# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Digital "
"signatures*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" are another powerful application of asymmetric key cryptography. They "
"provide authentication, integrity, and nonrepudiation enabled by the fact "
"that within AKC, entities possess unique private keys. The basic idea "
"underlying signature protocols is that senders of secure messages will "
"additionally *digitally sign* the messages using their unique private key. "
"The receiver will then verify the digital signature using the public key of "
"the sender. Within AKC, digital signatures can be implemented by using "
"algorithms specifically designed for that purpose or by using generic "
"cryptosystems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [*mga digital "
"signature*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191)"
" ay isa pang makapangyarihang aplikasyon ng asymmetric key cryptography. "
"Nagbibigay sila ng authentication, integridad, at nonrepudiation na pinagana"
" ng katotohanan na sa loob ng AKC, ang mga entidad ay nagtataglay ng "
"natatanging mga pribadong key. Ang pangunahing ideya sa likod ng mga "
"signature protocol ay ang mga nagpadala ng mga ligtas na mensahe ay "
"*digitally pipirmahan* din ang mga mensahe gamit ang kanilang natatanging "
"pribadong key. Ang tatanggap ay mag-ve-verify ng digital signature gamit ang"
" pampublikong key ng nagpadala. Sa loob ng AKC, ang mga digital signature ay"
" maaaring maipatupad sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga algorithm na espesyal"
" na idinisenyo para sa layuning iyon o sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga "
"generic na cryptosystem.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 4. Digital signatures with asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Larawan 4. Digital signatures gamit ang asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/dig_sig_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 4. Digital signatures  with asymmetric key cryptography*\n"
msgstr "*Larawan 4. Digital signatures gamit ang asymmetric key cryptography*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Dedicated digital signature algorithms {#dedicated-digital-signature-"
"algorithms}"
msgstr ""
"Mga dedicated na digital signature algorithm {#dedicated-digital-signature-"
"algorithms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Currently, the US Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) for digital"
" signatures is a dedicated scheme simply titled the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Somewhat similarly to the Diffie-Hellman protocol, the DSA uses the "
"algebraic properties of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponential</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The set of integers modulo a prime number, where the group "
"operation is modular multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group "
"are chosen in such a way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that"
" each element has a unique multiplicative inverse within the "
"group.\">multiplicative inverses</DefinitionTooltip> for signature "
"generation and verification.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasalukuyan, ang US Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) para "
"sa mga digital signature ay isang dedicated na scheme na simpleng "
"pinamagatang [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA). Medyo katulad sa Diffie-Hellman protocol, ginagamit ng DSA ang "
"algebraic na katangian ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang modular "
"exponentiation ay ang natitira kapag ang isang integer ay itinaas sa isang "
"kapangyarihan (exponent) at pagkatapos ay hinati sa isang numero (modulus). "
"Halimbawa $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponential</DefinitionTooltip> at "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang set ng mga integer modulo ng isang prime"
" number, kung saan ang group operation ay modular multiplication. Ang mga "
"element sa multiplicative group ay pinili sa ganitong paraan na sila ay "
"coprime sa modulus, na tinitiyak na ang bawat element ay may natatanging "
"multiplicative inverse sa loob ng group.\">multiplicative "
"inverses</DefinitionTooltip> para sa pagbuo at pag-verify ng signature.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [elliptic curve digital signature "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) is an ECC variant of DSA, providing the same functionality but with"
" significantly shorter keys. This results in improved efficiency, making it "
"a popular choice for systems with [resource "
"constraints](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [elliptic curve digital signature "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA) ay isang ECC variant ng DSA, na nagbibigay ng parehong "
"functionality ngunit may mas maikling mga key. Nagresulta ito sa pinahusay "
"na kahusayan, na ginagawa itong popular na pagpipilian para sa mga sistema "
"na may [limitasyon sa "
"resources](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Both DSA and ECDSA will be illustrated in more detail later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang parehong DSA at ECDSA ay ilalalarawan nang mas detalyado sa ibang "
"pagkakataon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Digital signature schemes using generic cryptosystems {#digital-signature-"
"schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"
msgstr ""
"Mga digital signature scheme gamit ang mga generic na cryptosystem "
"{#digital-signature-schemes-using-generic-cryptosystems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to dedicated algorithms, digital signatures can also be "
"generated using generic asymmetric cryptosystems, such as "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa mga dedicated na algorithm, ang mga digital signature ay maaari "
"ring mabuo gamit ang mga generic na asymmetric cryptosystem, tulad ng "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"RSA, which will be discussed in detail in a later section, also exploits "
"modular multiplicative inverses and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular "
"exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is raised to a power "
"(exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For example $x^e mod m$ "
".\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip> as fundamental operations but"
" combines them in a different sequence than DSA. In RSA, the signer "
"typically creates a hash of the message and then encrypts the hash with "
"their private key, creating the digital signature. Any party can then verify"
" this signature by decrypting it with the signer's public key and comparing "
"it with the hashed message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang RSA, na tatalakayin nang detalyado sa susunod na seksyon, ay gumagamit "
"din ng modular multiplicative inverses at <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang modular exponentiation ay ang natitira kapag ang isang "
"integer ay itinaas sa isang kapangyarihan (exponent) at pagkatapos ay hinati"
" sa isang numero (modulus). Halimbawa $x^e mod m$.\">modular "
"exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip> bilang mga pundamental na operasyon "
"ngunit pinagsama ang mga ito sa ibang pagkakasunud-sunod kaysa sa DSA. Sa "
"RSA, ang signer ay karaniwang gumagawa ng hash ng mensahe at pagkatapos ay "
"ine-encrypt ang hash gamit ang kanilang pribadong key, na lumilikha ng "
"digital signature. Ang sinumang partido ay maaaring i-verify ang signature "
"na ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-decrypt nito gamit ang pampublikong key ng "
"signer at pagkukumpara nito sa hashed na mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Applications of asymmetric key cryptography {#applications-of-asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Mga aplikasyon ng asymmetric key cryptography {#applications-of-asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Asymmetric key "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Something that is present or found everywhere, or something "
"that is widespread and commonly "
"encountered.\">ubiquitous</DefinitionTooltip> in modern digital technology "
"applications. The basic functionalities of AKC described above form the "
"building blocks of many higher-level application protocols, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [asymmetric key "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Public-"
"key_cryptography&oldid=1163952916) ay <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Isang "
"bagay na naroroon o matatagpuan kahit saan, o isang bagay na laganap at "
"karaniwang nakakatagpo.\">laganap</DefinitionTooltip> sa mga modernong "
"aplikasyon ng digital na teknolohiya. Ang mga pangunahing functionality ng "
"AKC na inilalarawan sa itaas ay bumubuo ng mga building block ng maraming "
"higher-level na application protocol, kabilang ang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Internet communication:** Secure communication over the internet, such as "
"HTTPS, relies heavily on asymmetric key cryptography. The Transport Layer "
"Security (TLS) and its predecessor, Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), use "
"asymmetric key cryptography during the initial handshake process to "
"establish a symmetric key, which is then used for the rest of the "
"communication session.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Komunikasyon sa internet:** Ang ligtas na komunikasyon sa internet, tulad "
"ng HTTPS, ay mabigat na umaasa sa asymmetric key cryptography. Ang Transport"
" Layer Security (TLS) at ang nauna nitong Secure Sockets Layer (SSL), ay "
"gumagamit ng asymmetric key cryptography sa panahon ng paunang proseso ng "
"handshake upang maitatag ang isang symmetric key, na ginagamit sa natitirang"
" bahagi ng session ng komunikasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Authentication:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used to create digital "
"signatures, allowing an entity to authenticate a digital document or message"
" as coming from a specific sender. This is used in many scenarios, from "
"verifying software updates to legally binding digital contracts.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Authentication:** Ang asymmetric key cryptography ay ginagamit upang "
"lumikha ng mga digital signature, na nagpapahintulot sa isang entidad na "
"i-authenticate ang isang digital na dokumento o mensahe na nagmula sa isang "
"partikular na nagpadala. Ginagamit ito sa maraming sitwasyon, mula sa pag-"
"verify ng mga software update hanggang sa mga legal na binding na digital na"
" kontrata.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Email encryption:** Email encryption protocols such as PGP (Pretty Good "
"Privacy) and its open-source alternative GPG (GNU Privacy Guard) use "
"asymmetric key cryptography to ensure that only the intended recipient can "
"read the email content.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Email encryption:** Ang mga email encryption protocol tulad ng PGP (Pretty"
" Good Privacy) at ang open-source na alternatibo nitong GPG (GNU Privacy "
"Guard) ay gumagamit ng asymmetric key cryptography upang matiyak na ang "
"nilalaman ng email ay mababasa lamang ng nilayong tatanggap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** SSH is a protocol for secure remote login and other "
"secure network services over an insecure network. It uses asymmetric key "
"cryptography to authenticate the server to the client and, optionally, the "
"client to the server.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Secure shell (SSH):** Ang SSH ay isang protocol para sa ligtas na remote "
"login at iba pang ligtas na serbisyo ng network sa pamamagitan ng isang "
"hindi ligtas na network. Gumagamit ito ng asymmetric key cryptography upang "
"ma-authenticate ang server sa client at, opsyonal, ang client sa server.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**VPN (virtual private network):** Asymmetric key encryption is used to "
"establish secure connections in VPNs, ensuring secure communication over "
"public networks.\n"
msgstr ""
"**VPN (virtual private network):** Ginagamit ang asymmetric key encryption "
"upang maitatag ang mga ligtas na koneksyon sa mga VPN, na tinitiyak ang "
"ligtas na komunikasyon sa pamamagitan ng mga pampublikong network.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Blockchain and cryptocurrencies:** Blockchain technologies, including "
"Bitcoin and Ethereum, use asymmetric key cryptography. For example, the "
"ownership of Bitcoin is established through digital signatures using "
"asymmetric key cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Blockchain at mga cryptocurrency:** Ang mga teknolohiya ng blockchain, "
"kabilang ang Bitcoin at Ethereum, ay gumagamit ng asymmetric key "
"cryptography. Halimbawa, ang pagmamay-ari ng Bitcoin ay itinatag sa "
"pamamagitan ng mga digital signature gamit ang asymmetric key "
"cryptography.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '7. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Certificate authorities:** Asymmetric key cryptography is used by "
"certificate authorities (CAs) to issue and sign digital certificates, which "
"are used in TLS communication, code signing, email encryption, and more. A "
"digital certificate binds a public key to a specific entity (for example, a "
"person or server).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga certificate authority:** Ang asymmetric key cryptography ay ginagamit "
"ng mga certificate authority (CA) upang mag-issue at pumirma ng mga digital "
"na sertipiko, na ginagamit sa TLS communication, code signing, email "
"encryption, at iba pa. Ang isang digital na sertipiko ay nagbubuklod ng "
"isang pampublikong key sa isang partikular na entidad (halimbawa, isang tao "
"o server).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-"
"key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Larawan 5. Pag-issue at pagpirma ng mga digital na sertipiko gamit ang "
"asymmetric key cryptography](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ca_akc.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 5. Issuing and signing digital certificates using asymmetric key "
"cryptography*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Larawan 5. Pag-issue at pagpirma ng mga digital na sertipiko gamit ang "
"asymmetric key cryptography*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of asymmetric key cryptography {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Seguridad ng asymmetric key cryptography {#security-of-asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Several cryptographic notions come together to enable secure asymmetric key "
"cryptography, including:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ilang cryptographic na konsepto ang nagsasama upang paganahin ang ligtas na "
"asymmetric key cryptography, kabilang ang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key secrecy**: The most basic security requirement of AKC is that "
"the private key remains secret. However, since the private key must be "
"mathematically linked to the public key, private key secrecy also requires "
"that it be computationally infeasible to derive the private key from "
"knowledge of the public key. Key generation schemes within AKC rely on "
"computationally hard mathematical problems to facilitate this requirement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Lihimang pribadong key**: Ang pinakabasikong kinakailangan sa seguridad ng"
" AKC ay ang pribadong key ay nananatiling lihim. Gayunpaman, dahil ang "
"pribadong key ay dapat na mathematically na naka-link sa pampublikong key, "
"ang pagiging lihim ng pribadong key ay nangangailangan din na hindi "
"maisagawa sa computational ang pagkuha ng pribadong key mula sa kaalaman ng "
"pampublikong key. Ang mga scheme ng pagbuo ng key sa loob ng AKC ay umaasa "
"sa mga computationally mahirap na mathematical na problema upang mapadali "
"ang kinakailangang ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Trapdoor functionality** In AKC, the encryption and decryption operations "
"involve different complementary keys from a single-key pair. Ciphertext "
"generated by encryption using one of the keys (for example the public key) "
"must be inscrutable to third parties while being easily decryptable by the "
"holder of the complementary key (in this case the private key). In other "
"words, encryption should resemble a [*trapdoor one-way "
"function*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" such that third parties cannot invert the operation and recover the plain "
"text but the private key provides a secret *trapdoor* that enables easy "
"inversion. Popular AKC algorithms use modular exponentiation to set up "
"trapdoor one-way function behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Trapdoor functionality**: Sa AKC, ang mga operasyon ng encryption at "
"decryption ay gumagamit ng iba't ibang complementary na mga key mula sa "
"isang key pair. Ang Ciphertext na nalikhang sa pamamagitan ng encryption "
"gamit ang isa sa mga key (halimbawa ang pampublikong key) ay dapat na hindi "
"maintindihan ng mga ikatlong partido habang madaling ma-decrypt ng may hawak"
" ng complementary na key (sa kasong ito ang pribadong key). Sa madaling "
"salita, ang encryption ay dapat na kahawig ng isang [*trapdoor one-way "
"function*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Trapdoor_function&oldid=1163913265)"
" upang ang mga ikatlong partido ay hindi maka-invert ng operasyon at mabawi "
"ang plain text ngunit ang pribadong key ay nagbibigay ng lihim na *trapdoor*"
" na nagbibigay-daan sa madaling pag-invert. Ang mga popular na AKC algorithm"
" ay gumagamit ng modular exponentiation upang maitatag ang gawi ng trapdoor "
"one-way function.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Randomness**: The key generation process should also exploit randomness to"
" ensure that keys are unpredictable, as any pattern or predictability in key"
" generation could be exploited by an attacker. Randomness is also used for "
"padding during encryption to generate semantically secure ciphertexts and "
"within digital signature schemes to produce unique signatures even when the "
"same message is signed multiple times. For this reason, the use of strong "
"random number generators is an important part of AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Randomness**: Ang proseso ng pagbuo ng key ay dapat ding gumamit ng "
"randomness upang matiyak na ang mga key ay hindi mahuhulaan, dahil ang "
"anumang pattern o predictability sa pagbuo ng key ay maaaring "
"mapagsamantalahan ng isang attacker. Ang randomness ay ginagamit din para sa"
" padding sa panahon ng encryption upang makabuo ng semantically secure na "
"mga ciphertext at sa loob ng mga digital signature scheme upang makagawa ng "
"natatanging mga signature kahit na ang parehong mensahe ay pinirmahan nang "
"maraming beses. Para sa kadahilanang ito, ang paggamit ng mga malakas na "
"random number generator ay isang mahalagang bahagi ng AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Large key size**: As in the case of SKC, large key sizes ensure protection"
" against brute force attacks. However, since large key sizes also increase "
"the computational cost of the encryption and decryption process, an optimal "
"solution needs to balance security and efficiency considerations. The "
"following table shows typical key sizes for various asymmetric key "
"cryptography protocols and applications:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Malaking laki ng key**: Tulad ng kaso ng SKC, ang malalaking laki ng key "
"ay nagbibigay ng proteksyon laban sa brute force attack. Gayunpaman, dahil "
"ang malalaking laki ng key ay nagpapataas din ng computational na gastos ng "
"proseso ng encryption at decryption, ang isang optimal na solusyon ay "
"kailangang balansehin ang mga pagsasaalang-alang sa seguridad at kahusayan. "
"Ang sumusunod na talahanayan ay nagpapakita ng mga tipikal na laki ng key "
"para sa iba't ibang asymmetric key cryptography protocol at aplikasyon:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Protocol | Typical Key Sizes (in bits)         | Application                    |\n"
"|----------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072, 4096 | Encryption, digital signatures |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072       | Digital signatures             |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                    | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Key exchange                   |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                  | Digital signatures             |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Protocol | Mga Tipikal na Laki ng Key (sa bits)  | Aplikasyon                       |\n"
"|----------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n"
"| RSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072, 4096   | Encryption, digital signatures   |\n"
"| DSA      | 1024 (deprecated), 2048, 3072         | Digital signatures               |\n"
"| DH       | 2048, 3072, 4096                      | Key exchange                     |\n"
"| ECDH     | 224, 256, 384, 521                    | Key exchange                     |\n"
"| ECDSA    | 224, 256, 384, 521                    | Digital signatures               |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key infrastructure**: In AKC, the private keys must be kept secret "
"by the owners while the public keys are shared. There needs to be a secure "
"mechanism to manage and distribute these public keys between users. *Public "
"key infrastructure* (PKI) provides a way to do this using *digital "
"certificates*. A digital certificate provides proof of identity of the owner"
" of the public key and is issued by a trusted authority like a certificate "
"authority(which is part of a PKI). Hence, PKI plays an integral part in the "
"security of modern application using AKC by enabling large-scale key "
"management (by creating, managing, distributing and revoking digital "
"certificates).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Public key infrastructure**: Sa AKC, ang mga pribadong key ay dapat na "
"panatilihing lihim ng mga may-ari habang ang mga pampublikong key ay "
"ibinabahagi. Kailangan ng isang ligtas na mekanismo upang pamahalaan at "
"ipamahagi ang mga pampublikong key na ito sa pagitan ng mga gumagamit. Ang "
"*Public key infrastructure* (PKI) ay nagbibigay ng isang paraan upang gawin "
"ito gamit ang mga *digital na sertipiko*. Ang isang digital na sertipiko ay "
"nagbibigay ng patunay ng pagkakakilanlan ng may-ari ng pampublikong key at "
"inilalabas ng isang pinagkakatiwalaang awtoridad tulad ng isang certificate "
"authority (na bahagi ng PKI). Kaya, ang PKI ay gumaganap ng mahalagang "
"bahagi sa seguridad ng modernong aplikasyon gamit ang AKC sa pamamagitan ng "
"pagpapagana ng large-scale na pamamahala ng key (sa pamamagitan ng paglikha,"
" pamamahala, pamamahagi at pagbawi ng mga digital na sertipiko).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security risks to asymmetric key cryptography {#security-risks-to-"
"asymmetric-key-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Mga panganib sa seguridad ng asymmetric key cryptography {#security-risks-"
"to-asymmetric-key-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As outlined in the above table, modern asymmetric key algorithms such as RSA"
" typically employ much larger key sizes than commonly used symmetric key "
"counterparts such as AES-128. Even the ECC-based protocols (ECDH and ECDSA) "
"that have smaller key sizes employ a minimum of at least 224 bits for keys. "
"This in turn implies that a brute force attack involving an exhaustive "
"search of the private key space to identify the correct key is "
"computationally intractable in the foreseeable future. This remains true "
"even if quantum computers were to be deployed for this task. Therefore, "
"attacks against AKC usually focus on exploiting other potential weaknesses "
"of specific cryptosystems. Some well-documented attack modes target:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng nakasaad sa talahanayan sa itaas, ang mga modernong asymmetric key "
"algorithm tulad ng RSA ay karaniwang gumagamit ng mas malalaking laki ng key"
" kaysa sa mga karaniwang ginagamit na symmetric key counterpart tulad ng "
"AES-128. Kahit ang mga ECC-based na protocol (ECDH at ECDSA) na may mas "
"maliliit na laki ng key ay gumagamit ng minimum na hindi bababa sa 224 bits "
"para sa mga key. Ito naman ay nagpapahiwatig na ang isang brute force attack"
" na kinabibilangan ng exhaustive search ng private key space upang matukoy "
"ang tamang key ay computationally intractable sa nakikitang hinaharap. "
"Nananatili itong totoo kahit na ang mga quantum computer ay ilalagay para sa"
" gawaing ito. Samakatuwid, ang mga pag-atake laban sa AKC ay karaniwang "
"nakatuon sa pagsasamantala ng iba pang posibleng kahinaan ng mga partikular "
"na cryptosystem. Ilang well-documented na attack mode ang nagta-target:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Algorithmic weakness** by using sophisticated mathematical and "
"computational means to undermine the hardness assumptions used to formulate "
"asymmetric key algorithms. For example, the security of RSA is predicated on"
" the difficulty of factoring large prime numbers, and recent computational "
"advances have [enabled successful factoring of 829-bit RSA "
"keys](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Therefore, 1024-bit RSA is currently deprecated. As will be discussed "
"later, the primary risk posed by quantum computers to AKC also falls into "
"this category.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kahinaan ng algorithm** sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng mga sopistikadong "
"mathematical at computational na paraan upang sirain ang mga hardness "
"assumption na ginamit upang bumuo ng mga asymmetric key algorithm. "
"Halimbawa, ang seguridad ng RSA ay nakabase sa kahirapan ng pag-factor ng "
"malalaking prime number, at ang mga kamakailang computational na pagsulong "
"ay [nagpahintulot ng matagumpay na pag-factor ng 829-bit na RSA "
"key](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)."
" Samakatuwid, ang 1024-bit na RSA ay kasalukuyang deprecated. Tulad ng "
"tatalakayin sa ibang pagkakataon, ang pangunahing panganib na inilalahad ng "
"mga quantum computer sa AKC ay napapabilang din sa kategoryang ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Imperfect randomness**, which can lead to weakness in the key generation "
"process. For example, if the random number generator used to create the keys"
" is flawed and generates keys that are not truly random, an attacker might "
"be able to predict the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hindi perpektong randomness**, na maaaring magdulot ng kahinaan sa proseso"
" ng pagbuo ng key. Halimbawa, kung ang random number generator na ginagamit "
"upang lumikha ng mga key ay may depekto at bumubuo ng mga key na hindi tunay"
" na random, maaaring matukoy ng isang attacker ang mga key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Implementation flaws** such as errors in the implementation of "
"cryptographic algorithms that inadvertently reveal information about the "
"keys. For example, incorrect padding can potentially reveal details about "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga depekto sa implementasyon** tulad ng mga pagkakamali sa implementasyon"
" ng mga cryptographic algorithm na hindi sinasadyang nagbubunyag ng "
"impormasyon tungkol sa mga key. Halimbawa, ang maling padding ay maaaring "
"potensyal na magbunyag ng mga detalye tungkol sa mga key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Side channels** that refer to information leakage from the physical system"
" that performs the cryptography. Such leaks could be in the form of timing "
"information, power consumption, or even sound, which can be exploited in a "
"so-called [*side-channel "
"attack*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). For example, analyzing how long "
"cryptographic operations take to execute could reveal the number of '1's in "
"a binary key. This seemingly innocent leakage significantly narrows the "
"search space, unveiling potential solutions to problems that initially "
"seemed insurmountable.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga side channel** na tumutukoy sa pagtagas ng impormasyon mula sa pisikal"
" na sistema na gumaganap ng cryptography. Ang ganitong mga pagtagas ay "
"maaaring nasa anyo ng impormasyon sa timing, pagkonsumo ng kuryente, o kahit"
" tunog, na maaaring mapagsamantalahan sa tinatawag na [*side-channel "
"attack*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Side-"
"channel_attack&oldid=1162235564). Halimbawa, ang pagsusuri kung gaano "
"katagal ang mga cryptographic na operasyon na isasagawa ay maaaring "
"magbunyag ng bilang ng mga '1' sa isang binary key. Ang tila walang masamang"
" pagtagas na ito ay makabuluhang nagpapaliit ng search space, na nagbubunyag"
" ng mga potensyal na solusyon sa mga problemang sa una ay tila hindi "
"malulutas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key exchange** by intercepting keys while they are being exchanged, such "
"as within a [*man-in-the-middle* "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). The DH protocol is susceptible to "
"MITM attacks if additional authentication steps are not incorporated.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Key exchange** sa pamamagitan ng pagharang sa mga key habang ito ay "
"ipinalpalitan, tulad ng sa loob ng isang [*man-in-the-middle* "
"attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Man-in-the-"
"middle_attack&oldid=1164741355) (MITM). Ang DH protocol ay madaling atakihin"
" ng MITM kung walang karagdagang hakbang ng authentication.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '6. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key storage** by aiming to steal keys from poorly secured storage. This "
"includes physical attacks such as manipulation or theft of storage "
"devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Key storage** sa pamamagitan ng paglalayon na magnakaw ng mga key mula sa "
"hindi ligtas na storage. Kasama dito ang mga pisikal na pag-atake tulad ng "
"manipulasyon o pagnanakaw ng mga device ng storage.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Securing asymmetric key cryptosystems against the variety of attacks that "
"are possible is therefore a significant task involving mathematical, "
"hardware, software, logistical, and legal considerations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pag-secure ng mga asymmetric key cryptosystem laban sa iba't ibang pag-"
"atake na posible ay samakatuwid isang makabuluhang gawain na kinabibilangan "
"ng mga mathematical, hardware, software, logistical, at legal na "
"pagsasaalang-alang.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA {#rsa}"
msgstr "RSA {#rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) algorithm is one of "
"the first public key cryptosystems and is widely used for secure data "
"transmission. It is a versatile cryptosystem in that it provides the "
"necessary operations to enable encryption, decryption, digital signatures, "
"and key exchange within a common framework.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [RSA (Rivest-Shamir-"
"Adleman)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/359340.359342) algorithm ay isa sa "
"mga unang public key cryptosystem at malawakang ginagamit para sa ligtas na "
"pagpapadala ng data. Isa itong versatile na cryptosystem dahil nagbibigay "
"ito ng mga kinakailangang operasyon upang paganahin ang encryption, "
"decryption, mga digital signature, at key exchange sa loob ng isang "
"karaniwang balangkas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this section, we will illustrate asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) using "
"RSA through simple examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa seksyong ito, ilalarawan natin ang asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) "
"gamit ang RSA sa pamamagitan ng mga simpleng halimbawa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use the standard scenario of two parties, Alice and Bob, who wish to"
" communicate securely using AKC.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamitin natin ang karaniwang senaryo ng dalawang partido, si Alice at Bob,"
" na gustong makipag-usap nang ligtas gamit ang AKC.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The RSA algorithm {#the-rsa-algorithm}"
msgstr "Ang RSA algorithm {#the-rsa-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The basic RSA algorithm involves four operations: key generation, key distribution, encryption, and decryption:\n"
"1. **Key generation:**\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangunahing RSA algorithm ay kinabibilangan ng apat na operasyon: key "
"generation, key distribution, encryption, at decryption:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Public and private keys are generated based on mathematical principles "
"around prime numbers, where calculating them is easy, but the reverse is "
"hard.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang mga pampubliko at pribadong key ay nalilikha batay sa mga "
"mathematical na prinsipyo tungkol sa mga prime number, kung saan ang "
"pagkalkula ng mga ito ay madali, ngunit ang kabaligtaran ay mahirap.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   We'll refer to these:\n"
"    - Public key: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Private key: $(d, n)$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ito ang ating gagamitin:\n"
"    - Pampublikong key: $(e, n)$\n"
"    - Pribadong key: $(d, n)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that $n$ is common to both public key and private key, and is known "
"as the modulus. We will need to use this later.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Tandaan na ang $n$ ay karaniwan sa parehong pampubliko at pribadong key, "
"at kilala bilang modulus. Kakailanganin nating gamitin ito sa ibang "
"pagkakataon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical na detalye\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose two distinct prime numbers, $p$ and $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng dalawang natatanging prime number, $p$ at $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "chosen at random (for security).\n"
msgstr "pinili nang random (para sa seguridad).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"They should be similar in magnitude, but differ in length by a few digits, "
"to make factoring harder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dapat silang magkatulad sa magnitude, ngunit mag-iiba ng ilang digit sa "
"haba, upang gawing mas mahirap ang pag-factor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime numbers can be efficiently chosen using a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm to determine whether a given number is prime. This"
" is relatively easy computationally compared to factorization.\">primality "
"test</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga prime number ay maaaring mahusay na mapili gamit ang isang "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Isang algorithm upang matukoy kung ang isang"
" ibinigay na numero ay prime. Ito ay medyo madali sa computational na paraan"
" kumpara sa factorization.\">primality test</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $n = p*q$.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang $n = p*q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$n$ is the modulus for both the public and private keys.\n"
msgstr "Ang $n$ ay ang modulus para sa parehong pampubliko at pribadong key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang totient ay isang numero, "
"o mga numero, na hindi mas malaki kaysa sa ibinigay na numero, at medyo "
"prime dito, na walang mga salik na karaniwan.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang Greek na simbolo, phi, na madalas na "
"ginagamit upang ipahiwatig ang Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n) = (p-1)*(q-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The totient is meant to be kept secret and typically discarded after key "
"generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang totient ay dapat na panatilihing lihim at karaniwang itinatapon "
"pagkatapos ng key generation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an integer $e$ such that $1 < e < $ <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\"> $φ$ </DefinitionTooltip> $(n)$ and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The"
" greek symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng integer na $e$ upang $1 < e < $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang"
" Greek na simbolo, phi, na madalas na ginagamit upang ipahiwatig ang Euler's"
" totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ at <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - ang pinakamalaking positibong buong "
"numero na maaaring hatiin ang dalawa o higit pang mga ibinigay na buong "
"numero\">$gcd$</DefinitionTooltip>$(e, $<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang "
"Greek na simbolo, phi, na madalas na ginagamit upang ipahiwatig ang Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)) = 1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that is, $e$ and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, "
"often used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ "
"should be <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that have a greatest "
"common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime because only 1 can "
"divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"ibig sabihin, ang $e$ at <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang Greek na "
"simbolo, phi, na madalas na ginagamit upang ipahiwatig ang Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ ay dapat na <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Dalawang numero na may greatest common divisor na 1. Halimbawa,"
" ang 3 at 13 ay coprime dahil 1 lamang ang makakahatid sa pareho "
"nila.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $e$ forms the public key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> and is typically chosen as a small "
"number for computational efficiency.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang numerong $e$ na ito ay bumubuo ng pampublikong key <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang bilang ng beses na ang isang numero ay pinarami sa sarili "
"nito.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> at karaniwang pinipili bilang isang "
"maliit na numero para sa computational na kahusayan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The prime number $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ is often used.\n"
msgstr "Ang prime number na $65537 = 2^{16} + 1$ ay madalas na ginagamit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $d$ to satisfy the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or "
"equivalence ie. all behaving in the same way.\">congruence "
"relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek "
"symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang $d$ upang masiyahan ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Pagkakatulad, o pagkakapantay-pantay, ibig sabihin lahat ay "
"kumikilos sa parehong paraan.\">congruence relation</DefinitionTooltip> na "
"$d*e ≡ 1 ($<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang modulus ay ang natitira "
"pagkatapos ng paghahati sa tinukoy na halaga. Ang modulo ay ang operasyon ng"
" paggawa nito.\">$mod$</DefinitionTooltip><DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang Greek na simbolo, phi, na madalas na ginagamit upang "
"ipahiwatig ang Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n))$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, $d$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as "
"reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by the number given, results in "
"a value of 1.\">multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibig sabihin, ang $d$ ay ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Kilala rin "
"bilang reciprocal, isang numero, na kapag pinarami sa ibinigay na numero, ay"
" nagresulta sa halaga ng 1.\">multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> ng "
"$e$ modulo <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang Greek na simbolo, phi, na "
"madalas na ginagamit upang ipahiwatig ang Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is more efficiently computed using the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest common divisor of "
"two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay mas mahusay na kinakalkula gamit ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Isang mahusay na paraan ng pagkalkula ng greatest common "
"divisor ng dalawang buong numero. Nagpapabuti ito sa orihinal na Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '       - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This number $d$ is the private key <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"number of times a number is multiplied by "
"itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang numerong $d$ na ito ay ang pribadong key <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang bilang ng beses na ang isang numero ay pinarami sa sarili "
"nito.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The public key consists of $(e, n)$, and the private key is $(d, n)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pampublikong key ay binubuo ng $(e, n)$, at ang pribadong key ay $(d, "
"n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Key distribution:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Key distribution:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key $(e, n)$ is made public to those who may wish to send a "
"message\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pampublikong key $(e, n)$ ay ginagawang pampubliko para sa mga gustong "
"magpadala ng mensahe\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The private key $(d, n)$ is kept secret.\n"
msgstr "Ang pribadong key $(d, n)$ ay pinapanatiling lihim.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Encryption:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to send a message $M$ to Bob. In this case a simple integer\n"
msgstr ""
"Gustong magpadala ni Alice ng mensaheng $M$ kay Bob. Sa kasong ito ay isang "
"simpleng integer\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice uses Bob's public key $(e, n)$ to encrypt the message into ciphertext "
"$C$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ni Alice ang pampublikong key ni Bob $(e, n)$ upang i-encrypt ang "
"mensahe bilang ciphertext $C$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical detail\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical na detalye\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$M$ is an <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"We consider an integer in this "
"example as the simplest case. Any message can be converted into an integer "
"based representation.\">integer</DefinitionTooltip> $0 ≤ M < n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $M$ ay isang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Isinasaalang-alang natin "
"ang isang integer sa halimbawang ito bilang ang pinakasimpleng kaso. Ang "
"anumang mensahe ay maaaring ma-convert sa isang integer-based na "
"representasyon.\">integer</DefinitionTooltip> na $0 ≤ M < n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, where $C$ is the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr "$C ≡ M^e (mod n)$, kung saan ang $C$ ay ang ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Decryption:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Decryption:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob receives the ciphertext $C$\n"
msgstr "Natanggap ni Bob ang ciphertext $C$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob uses his private key $(d, n)$ to decrypt the message back into message "
"$M$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit ni Bob ang kanyang pribadong key $(d, n)$ upang i-decrypt ang "
"mensahe pabalik sa mensaheng $M$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"
msgstr "$M ≡ C^d (mod n)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"This is the basic outline of RSA. In practice, [more sophisticated padding schemes](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) are applied to the plain text $M$ before encryption to ensure that equal plain texts result in different ciphertexts. This prevents a range of possible attacks against naive implementations of RSA and enables <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"Ito ang pangunahing balangkas ng RSA. Sa praktiko, [mas sopistikadong mga padding scheme](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577) ang inilalapat sa plain text na $M$ bago ang encryption upang matiyak na ang mga pantay na plain text ay nagresulta sa iba't ibang ciphertext. Pinipigilan nito ang isang hanay ng mga posibleng pag-atake laban sa mga naive na implementasyon ng RSA at nagpapagana ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Sa pamamagitan lamang ng ciphertext, at anumang kaugnay na pampublikong impormasyon (tulad ng pampublikong key para sa asymmetric key cryptography), at ang isang kalaban ay hindi makakakuha ng kahit bahagyang impormasyon mula sa plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of RSA in Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasyon ng RSA sa Python {#illustration-of-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate a simple example of the RSA "
"algorithm using small integers and then demonstrate practical key "
"distribution and digital signature applications using Python libraries "
"implementing RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga sumusunod na code cell, ipinapakita natin ang isang simpleng "
"halimbawa ng RSA algorithm gamit ang maliliit na integer, at pagkatapos ay "
"nagpapakita ng praktikal na key distribution at digital signature na mga "
"aplikasyon gamit ang mga Python library na nagpapatupad ng RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Note: In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Tandaan: Sa seksyong ito, ipapakita natin ang mga kalkulasyong matematikal nang detalyado bilang bahagi ng Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "RSA key generation {#rsa-key-generation}"
msgstr "Paglikha ng RSA key {#rsa-key-generation}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's step through a simple instance of the RSA algorithm employing small "
"prime numbers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sundan natin ang isang simpleng halimbawa ng RSA algorithm gamit ang "
"maliliit na prime na numero.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will need to be able to compute the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> of two integers, as it will be needed to test "
"whether two integers are <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Two numbers that "
"have a greatest common divisor of 1. For example, 3 and 13 are coprime "
"because only 1 can divide both of them.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kakailanganin nating makalkula ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest "
"Common Divisor - ang pinakamalaking positibong buong numerong makakapaghatid"
" ng dalawa o higit pang ibinigay na buong numero.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> ng dalawang integer, dahil kailangan ito para "
"masuri kung ang dalawang integer ay <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Dalawang"
" numero na ang greatest common divisor ay 1. Halimbawa, ang 3 at 13 ay "
"coprime dahil ang 1 lamang ang makakahatid sa "
"dalawa.\">coprime</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will explain one simple way to calculate this, but it is much more "
"efficient with larger integers to use the `math.gcd` python function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magpapaliwanag tayo ng isang simpleng paraan para kalkulahin ito, ngunit mas"
" mahusay para sa malalaking integer ang paggamit ng `math.gcd` na Python "
"function.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first phase of the RSA workflow is key generation. This is initiated by "
"choosing two prime numbers, which are meant to be kept secret by the entity "
"generating the keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang yugto ng RSA workflow ay ang paglikha ng key. Nagsisimula ito sa "
"pagpili ng dalawang prime na numero, na dapat itago ng entity na gumagawa ng"
" mga key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left "
"over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing"
" this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, which is simply the product of the"
" two chosen primes, is computed. This modulus will be published as part of "
"the public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, kinakalkula ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang modulus ay ang "
"natitirang halaga pagkatapos hatiin sa tinukoy na halaga. Ang modulo ay ang "
"operasyon ng paggawa nito.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$, na simpleng "
"produkto ng dalawang piniling prime. Ang modulus na ito ay ilalathala bilang"
" bahagi ng public key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Euler <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The totient is a number, or "
"numbers, that are not greater than the given number, and are relatively "
"prime to it, having no factors in common.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> is computed"
" next, as it is needed for the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an "
"integer $a$, and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the"
" case for coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> "
"operation used to determine the keys in RSA. $phi$ is also kept secret and "
"typically discarded after key generation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Euler <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang totient ay isang numero, o mga"
" numero, na hindi mas malaki kaysa sa ibinigay na numero, at medyo prime "
"dito, na walang mga salik na magkakatulad.\">totient</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function na <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang Greek na simbolo, phi, na "
"madalas gamitin para isaad ang Euler's "
"totient.\">$\\varphi(n)$</DefinitionTooltip> ay kinakalkula susunod, dahil "
"kailangan ito para sa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ibinigay ang isang "
"integer $a$, at modulus $m$, ang natira mula sa ax/m ay 1. Ito ay totoo "
"lamang para sa mga coprime.\">modular multiplicative "
"inverse</DefinitionTooltip> na operasyon na ginagamit para matukoy ang mga "
"key sa RSA. Ang $phi$ ay itinatago rin nang lihim at karaniwang itinatapon "
"pagkatapos ng key generation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We are now ready to calculate the public and private keys. In RSA, each of "
"these is specified by a tuple of two integers. The first entry in each tuple"
" is a distinct integer, and the second entry is the modulus $n$ that is "
"common to both keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Handa na tayo ngayon na kalkulahin ang mga public at private key. Sa RSA, "
"ang bawat isa sa mga ito ay tinukoy ng tuple ng dalawang integer. Ang unang "
"entry sa bawat tuple ay isang natatanging integer, at ang pangalawang entry "
"ay ang modulus $n$ na karaniwan sa parehong key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first entry in the public key can be any integer greater than 1 that is "
"coprime to $phi$. Two integers are coprime if their <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole numbers.\">greatest common "
"divisor</DefinitionTooltip> is 1. So we use the `math.gcd` function find an "
"integer $e$ coprime to $phi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang entry sa public key ay maaaring maging anumang integer na mas "
"malaki sa 1 na coprime sa $phi$. Ang dalawang integer ay coprime kung ang "
"kanilang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - ang "
"pinakamalaking positibong buong numerong makakapaghatid ng dalawa o higit "
"pang ibinigay na buong numero.\">greatest common divisor</DefinitionTooltip>"
" ay 1. Kaya ginagamit natin ang `math.gcd` function para mahanap ang integer"
" $e$ na coprime sa $phi$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key requires an integer $d$, which is the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Also known as reciprocal, a number, which when multiplied by "
"the number given, results in a value of 1.\">multiplicative "
"inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of $e$ modulo $phi$; that is, it satisfies the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruency relation</DefinitionTooltip> $d*e\\equiv 1 "
"\\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. For this simple illustration where we are dealing with"
" small integers, we can just loop over the positive integers to locate a "
"suitable $d$. In realistic settings, the computationally efficient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the greatest"
" common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original Euclidean "
"algorithm.\">extended Euclidean algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> is used for "
"this purpose.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang private key ay nangangailangan ng integer $d$, na siyang "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Kilala rin bilang reciprocal, isang numero "
"na kapag pinarami sa ibinigay na numero, ay nagbubunga ng halagang "
"1.\">multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> ng $e$ modulo $phi$; ibig "
"sabihin, nasasabay ito sa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pagkakatulad, o "
"pagkakapantay-pantay, ibig sabihin lahat ay kumikilos sa parehong "
"paraan.\">congruency relation</DefinitionTooltip> na $d*e\\equiv 1 "
"\\pmod{\\varphi(n)}$. Para sa simpleng ilustrasyong ito na gumagamit ng "
"maliliit na integer, maaari tayong mag-loop sa mga positibong integer para "
"mahanap ang angkop na $d$. Sa mga realitibong setting, ang computationally "
"efficient na <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Isang mahusay na paraan ng "
"pagkalkula ng greatest common divisor ng dalawang buong numero. Nagpapabuti "
"ito sa orihinal na Euclidean algorithm.\">extended Euclidean "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> ang ginagamit para sa layuning ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now form the tuples $(e, n), (d, n)$, which form the public and private "
"keys respectively. The public key is then published, while the private key "
"is kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Binubuo na natin ngayon ang mga tuple $(e, n), (d, n)$, na nagbibigay ng "
"public at private key ayon sa pagkakasunod. Ang public key ay ilalathala, "
"habang ang private key ay itinatago nang lihim.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption and decryption in RSA use the [modular exponentiation "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Further, the public and private keys are complementary in that either can "
"be used to encrypt a message that the other can then decrypt.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang encryption at decryption sa RSA ay gumagamit ng [modular exponentiation "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Modular_exponentiation&oldid=1160764843)."
" Bukod dito, ang mga public at private key ay magkakomplemento sa lawak na "
"ang alinman sa mga ito ay maaaring gamitin para i-encrypt ang isang mensahe "
"na maaaring i-decrypt ng isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we illustrate the case where the public key $(e,n)$ is used for "
"encryption and the private key $(d, n)$ is used for decryption by defining a"
" Python function for each operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ipinapakita natin ang kaso kung saan ang public key $(e,n)$ ay "
"ginagamit para sa encryption at ang private key $(d, n)$ ay ginagamit para "
"sa decryption sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy ng Python function para sa bawat "
"operasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then encrypt and decrypt an integer message $msg$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos ay ine-encrypt at dine-decrypt natin ang isang integer na mensahe"
" $msg$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the small integers used above are useful to easily outline the core "
"ideas in the RSA algorithm, in real applications RSA requires the use of "
"very large integers. For example, 2048-bit RSA involves the use of a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left over after"
" dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ that is 2048 bits long, the decimal "
"integer equivalents of which are around 10$^616$. These truly enormous "
"numbers are necessary for the practical security of RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang ang maliliit na integer na ginamit sa itaas ay kapaki-pakinabang para"
" madaling ibalangkas ang mga pangunahing ideya sa RSA algorithm, sa mga "
"tunay na aplikasyon ang RSA ay nangangailangan ng paggamit ng napakalaking "
"integer. Halimbawa, ang 2048-bit RSA ay gumagamit ng <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang modulus ay ang natitirang halaga pagkatapos hatiin sa "
"tinukoy na halaga. Ang modulo ay ang operasyon ng paggawa "
"nito.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$ na 2048 bits ang haba, na ang "
"katumbas na decimal integer ay humigit-kumulang 10$^616$. Ang mga tunay na "
"napakalaking numerong ito ay kinakailangan para sa praktikal na seguridad ng"
" RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Symmetric key exchange with RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"
msgstr ""
"Palitan ng symmetric key gamit ang RSA {#symmetric-key-exchange-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed previously, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Asynchronous key "
"encryption.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> enables two parties who wish to "
"communicate to securely establish a *shared secret*, which can be used, for "
"instance, as the secret key for subsequent symmetric encryption of bulk "
"plain text.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng tinalakay nang mas maaga, ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Asynchronous key encryption.\">AKC</DefinitionTooltip> ay "
"nagbibigay-daan sa dalawang partidong gustong makipag-communicate na ligtas "
"na magtatag ng isang *shared secret*, na maaaring gamitin, halimbawa, bilang"
" secret key para sa kasunod na symmetric encryption ng bulk na plain text.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us consider the following scenario. Alice and Bob want to use "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> to encrypt and decrypt messages. "
"However, before this process can be initialized, they need to agree on a "
"common secret key. One option is for one party — say, Alice — to generate a "
"secret key and then securely transmit it to Bob. To achieve this secure "
"transfer, Alice decides to use RSA as the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Key encapsulation mechanism. Secures a symmetric key by use of "
"asymmetric key encryption. A simple approach is to encrypt a random "
"symmetric key using a public key, but more advanced & secure kems are "
"available, and new ones continually developed.\">key encapsulation "
"mechanism</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang natin ang sumusunod na sitwasyon. Gusto ni Alice at Bob na "
"gumamit ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> para mag-encrypt at mag-decrypt ng mga"
" mensahe. Gayunpaman, bago masimula ang prosesong ito, kailangan nilang "
"magkasundo sa isang karaniwang secret key. Isang opsyon ay para sa isang "
"partido — sabihin nating si Alice — na lumikha ng secret key at pagkatapos "
"ay ligtas na ipadala ito kay Bob. Para makamit ang ligtas na paglilipat na "
"ito, nagpasya si Alice na gamitin ang RSA bilang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Key encapsulation mechanism. Sinisigurado ang isang symmetric "
"key sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng asymmetric key encryption. Ang isang "
"simpleng diskarte ay ang pag-encrypt ng isang random na symmetric key gamit "
"ang isang public key, ngunit may mga mas advanced at ligtas na KEM na "
"magagamit, at patuloy na binubuo ang mga bago.\">key encapsulation "
"mechanism</DefinitionTooltip> (KEM).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This involves the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Kabilang sa prosesong ito ang mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice generates a random symmetric key, which she intends to share "
"with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, lumilikha si Alice ng isang random na symmetric key, na balak niyang "
"ibahagi kay Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob generates an asymmetric key pair and makes his public key "
"available on a suitable channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, gumagawa si Bob ng asymmetric key pair at ginagawa ang kanyang "
"public key available sa isang angkop na channel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the symmetric key, thus "
"encapsulating it in a ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, ginagamit ni Alice ang public key ni Bob para i-encrypt ang "
"symmetric key, kaya ikinakapsul ito sa isang ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice broadcasts the ciphertext over a reliable but not necessarily "
"secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ibinabahagi ni Alice ang ciphertext sa isang maaasahang ngunit "
"hindi naman kailangang ligtas na channel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob receives the ciphertext and decrypts it using his private key. "
"He now has access to the symmetric key generated by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, tinatanggap ni Bob ang ciphertext at dine-decrypt ito gamit ang "
"kanyang private key. Mayroon na siyang access sa symmetric key na nilikha ni"
" Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with "
"RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/key_exchange_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Symmetric key exchange with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Figure 1. Palitan ng symmetric key gamit ang RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Padding-based key-exchange example in Python {#padding-based-key-exchange-"
"example-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa ng padding-based na key exchange sa Python {#padding-based-key-"
"exchange-example-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A practical workflow utilizing RSA for padding-based non-interactive key "
"exchange is now illustrated using the ``cryptography`` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang praktikal na workflow na gumagamit ng RSA para sa padding-based na "
"non-interactive key exchange ay ipinapakita ngayon gamit ang "
"``cryptography`` na Python library.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Import necessary modules from the ``cryptography`` Python library. If "
"needed, this library can be installed using the command ``pip install "
"cryptography``.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-import ang mga kinakailangang module mula sa ``cryptography`` na Python "
"library. Kung kinakailangan, ang library na ito ay maaaring i-install gamit "
"ang command na ``pip install cryptography``.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then generates a random secret key, which she intends to transmit to "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, lumilikha si Alice ng random na secret key, na balak niyang "
"ipadala kay Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the ``rsa`` module from the ``cryptography`` library, Bob generates a "
"key pair and then broadcasts his public key. Any one can intercept the "
"public key and read off the public numbers $(e,n)$ that form the key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang ``rsa`` module mula sa ``cryptography`` library, gumagawa si Bob "
"ng key pair at pagkatapos ay ibinabahagi ang kanyang public key. Maaaring "
"maharang ng sinuman ang public key at mabasa ang mga public number $(e,n)$ "
"na bumubuo sa key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, we assume Alice has received the public key broadcast by Bob."
" Alice's ``symmetric_key`` above can now be encrypted using Bob's public key"
" to produce the ciphertext. In a realistic setting, Alice will also use "
"additional <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The addition of data to the "
"beginning, middle, or end of a message. Often used in block ciphers to fill "
"out blocks with insufficient data up to the required "
"size.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> methods such as "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" to ensure <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"With only the ciphertext, and any"
" relevant public information (such as public key for asymmetric key "
"cryptography), and adversary cannot retrieve even partial information from "
"the plaintext.\">semantic security</DefinitionTooltip> for her "
"communications with Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa puntong ito, ipinapalagay nating natanggap ni Alice ang public key na "
"ibinahagi ni Bob. Ang ``symmetric_key`` ni Alice sa itaas ay maaari nang "
"i-encrypt gamit ang public key ni Bob para makagawa ng ciphertext. Sa isang "
"realitibong setting, gagamit din si Alice ng karagdagang mga paraan ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang pagdaragdag ng data sa simula, gitna, o "
"dulo ng isang mensahe. Madalas na ginagamit sa block cipher para punan ang "
"mga block na may kulang na data hanggang sa kinakailangang "
"laki.\">padding</DefinitionTooltip> tulad ng "
"[OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" para matiyak ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Sa ciphertext lamang, at "
"anumang kaugnay na pampublikong impormasyon (tulad ng public key para sa "
"asymmetric key cryptography), hindi maaaring makakuha ng kahit bahagyang "
"impormasyon mula sa plaintext ang isang kalaban.\">semantic "
"security</DefinitionTooltip> para sa kanyang mga komunikasyon kay Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext over an open channel, confident that "
"only Bob with the corresponding private key will be able to decrypt it. We "
"assume Bob has received the ciphertext and can now decrypt it using his "
"confidential private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinabahagi ni Alice ang ciphertext sa isang bukas na channel, tiwala na si "
"Bob lamang na may kaukulang private key ang makakapag-decrypt nito. "
"Ipinapalagay nating natanggap ni Bob ang ciphertext at maaari na itong "
"i-decrypt gamit ang kanyang kumpidensyal na private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point, Alice and Bob both have access to the secret symmetric key, "
"which they can use for <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip> applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa puntong ito, parehong si Alice at Bob ay may access na sa secret "
"symmetric key, na maaari nilang gamitin para sa mga aplikasyon ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Symmetric key "
"encryption.\">SKC</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simulating a Key Encapsulation Mechanism with RSA in Python {#simulating-a-"
"key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Paggaya sa Key Encapsulation Mechanism gamit ang RSA sa Python {#simulating-"
"a-key-encapsulation-mechanism-with-rsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following workflow, we illustrate the use of RSA to simulate a Key "
"Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) whereby a sufficiently long random secret "
"message is securely exchanged and subsequently converted into a shared-"
"secret of the appropriate length using a KDF.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sumusunod na workflow, ipinapakita natin ang paggamit ng RSA para gayahin"
" ang isang Key Encapsulation Mechanism (KEM) kung saan isang sapat na mahaba"
" random na secret na mensahe ay ligtas na ipinagpapalit at kasunod na kino-"
"convert sa isang shared secret ng angkop na haba gamit ang isang KDF.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once again Alice and Bob want to establish a shared secret non-interactively"
" and Alice is the party that decides which secret to use.\n"
msgstr ""
"Muli, gusto ni Alice at Bob na magtatag ng isang shared secret nang hindi "
"nagta-transact nang direkta, at si Alice ang partido na nagpapasya kung "
"aling secret ang gagamitin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start by importing some necessary Python libraries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagsisimula tayo sa pag-import ng ilang kinakailangang Python library.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob then generates his RSA key pair and broadcasts his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, gumagawa si Bob ng kanyang RSA key pair at ibinabahagi ang "
"kanyang public key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice first generates a long random secret from which the shared secret will"
" be eventually derived. In a pure "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965),"
" the long secret will be a random element from the algebraic structure "
"underlying the cryptosystem. In the case of 2048-bit RSA, this would be a "
"random integer modulo the 2048-bit RSA modulus. As such a pure KEM does not "
"require additional padding but in this example we are only simulating a KEM "
"using RSA and the `cryptography` library requires the use of padding when "
"encrypting with RSA. So we will use a somewhat shorter long secret which "
"nevertheless is much longer than a standard 256-bit AES key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Unang gumagawa si Alice ng isang mahabang random na secret mula sa kung saan"
" sa kalaunan ay matatamo ang shared secret. Sa isang purong "
"[KEM](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965),"
" ang mahabang secret ay magiging isang random na elemento mula sa algebraic "
"na istruktura na pinagbabatayan ng cryptosystem. Sa kaso ng 2048-bit RSA, "
"ito ay magiging isang random na integer na modulo ng 2048-bit RSA modulus. "
"Dahil ang isang purong KEM ay hindi nangangailangan ng karagdagang padding "
"ngunit sa halimbawang ito ay gina-gaya lamang natin ang isang KEM gamit ang "
"RSA at ang `cryptography` library ay nangangailangan ng paggamit ng padding "
"kapag nag-e-encrypt gamit ang RSA. Kaya gagamit tayo ng medyo mas maikling "
"mahabang secret na gayunpaman ay mas mahaba pa rin kaysa sa isang karaniwang"
" 256-bit AES key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next Alice encrypts the long secret using Bob's public key and the encrypted"
" secret is communicated to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, ine-encrypt ni Alice ang mahabang secret gamit ang public key ni "
"Bob at ang naka-encrypt na secret ay ipinagpapalit kay Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob decrypt's the encrypted secret received from Alice using his private "
"key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dine-decrypt ni Bob ang naka-encrypt na secret na natanggap mula kay Alice "
"gamit ang kanyang private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally both Alice and Bob separately apply an agreed upon [Key Derivation "
"Function](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) on the long secret to derive the symmetric key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, parehong si Alice at Bob ay magkahiwalay na nag-aaplay ng "
"napagkasunduang [Key Derivation "
"Function](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_derivation_function&oldid=1165650237)"
" (KDF) sa mahabang secret para makuha ang symmetric key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the process involves a hashing protocol and the use of a random "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Regarding password hashing, the idea that "
"salt enhances/makes a food unique is the same idea of how adding salt in "
"this context makes our password unique, distinctive, and hard to "
"reproduce.\">*salt*</DefinitionTooltip> which ensures uniqueness and "
"unpredictability of the shared symmetric key in case the long secret is ever"
" reused (not recommended). However the *salt* itself does not have to be "
"secret and once it is randomly generated, say by Alice in this example, it "
"can be broadcasted to Bob alongside the encrypted long secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang proseso ay kinabibilangan ng isang hashing protocol at ang "
"paggamit ng isang random na <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Tungkol sa "
"password hashing, ang ideya na ang asin ay nagpapahusay/nagpapatangi ng "
"pagkain ay parehong ideya ng kung paano ang pagdaragdag ng asin sa "
"kontekstong ito ay ginagawang natatangi ang ating password, nagpapaiba nito,"
" at nagpapahirap na maulit o ma-reproduce ito.\">*salt*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"na tinitiyak ang pagiging natatangi at hindi mahulaan ng shared symmetric "
"key sakaling ang mahabang secret ay muling gamitin (hindi inirerekomenda). "
"Gayunpaman ang *salt* mismo ay hindi kailangang maging lihim at kapag random"
" itong nagawa, sabihin nating ni Alice sa halimbawang ito, maaari itong "
"ibahagi kay Bob kasabay ng naka-encrypt na mahabang secret.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will assume therefore that both Alice and Bob have access to the same "
"random *salt*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapalagay nating parehong si Alice at Bob ay may access sa parehong "
"random na *salt*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"
msgstr "Mga digital signature gamit ang RSA {#digital-signatures-with-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will now extend the above confidential communication scenario with Alice "
"and Bob to one that also includes validation with the help of a [digital "
"signature](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"
msgstr ""
"Palawakin na natin ngayon ang sitwasyon ng kumpidensyal na komunikasyon sa "
"pagitan ni Alice at Bob para isama rin ang validation sa tulong ng isang "
"[digital "
"signature](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_signature&oldid=1161173191).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, Alice will confidentially send a message encapsulating a "
"symmetric key to Bob, but she will also digitally sign the message so that "
"Bob, upon receiving the message, can verify that it was Alice who originated"
" it and that the contents of the message were not tampered with during "
"transmission.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng dati, lihim na magpapadala si Alice ng mensahe na naglalaman ng "
"symmetric key kay Bob, ngunit maglalagay din siya ng digital signature sa "
"mensahe para mapatunayan ni Bob, sa pagtanggap ng mensahe, na si Alice ang "
"nagpadala nito at na ang nilalaman ng mensahe ay hindi binago sa panahon ng "
"pagpapadala.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, it is desirable to enable validation without compromising "
"confidentiality whereby any interested party is able to verify the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is "
"protected against unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is "
"from the source it claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"and establish non-repudiation with respect to a given communication, even if"
" that party does not have access to the actual plain text message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pangkalahatan, kanais-nais na mapagana ang validation nang hindi "
"nakompromiso ang kumpidensyalidad kung saan ang anumang interesadong partido"
" ay may kakayahang i-verify ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang "
"integridad ay napanatili kapag ang isang mensahe ay protektado laban sa "
"hindi awtorisadong pagbabago.\">integridad</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang pagiging tunay ay ang patunay na ang "
"isang mensahe ay nagmula sa pinagmulan na inaangkin nito.\">pagiging "
"tunay</DefinitionTooltip>, at magtayo ng non-repudiation kaugnay ng isang "
"ibinigay na komunikasyon, kahit na ang partidong iyon ay walang access sa "
"aktwal na plain text na mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will consider this general setting which then involves the following "
"steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Isasaalang-alang natin ang pangkalahatang setting na ito na kinabibilangan "
"ng mga sumusunod na hakbang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, both Bob and Alice make their public keys available over an open "
"channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, parehong si Bob at Alice ay ginagawang available ang kanilang mga "
"public key sa isang bukas na channel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice encrypts the plain text using Bob's public key, creating a "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ine-encrypt ni Alice ang plain text gamit ang public key ni Bob,"
" na lumilikha ng isang ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice creates a hash of the ciphertext with a *hash function* and "
"further encrypts the resulting hashed ciphertext using her private key. This"
" encrypted hash is the *signature*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, gumagawa si Alice ng hash ng ciphertext gamit ang isang *hash "
"function* at dagdag na ine-encrypt ang nagresultang na-hash na ciphertext "
"gamit ang kanyang private key. Ang naka-encrypt na hash na ito ay ang "
"*signature*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then transmits both the ciphertext and the signature over an "
"open channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ipinapadala ni Alice ang parehong ciphertext at signature sa "
"isang bukas na channel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob uses Alice's public key to decrypt the signature, revealing the "
"hashed ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ginagamit ni Bob ang public key ni Alice para i-decrypt ang "
"signature, inilalantad ang na-hash na ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, since Bob also has access to the ciphertext itself, he uses the same "
"hash function used by Alice to recreate a second instance of the hashed "
"ciphertext. If the latter matches the one obtained by decrypting Alice's "
"signature, then the message is validated, even though the ciphertext itself "
"has not yet been decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, dahil mayroon ding access si Bob sa ciphertext mismo, ginagamit "
"niya ang parehong hash function na ginamit ni Alice para muling lumikha ng "
"pangalawang instance ng na-hash na ciphertext. Kung ang huli ay tumutugma sa"
" nakuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-decrypt ng signature ni Alice, ang mensahe ay "
"na-validate, kahit na ang ciphertext mismo ay hindi pa na-decrypt.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob, having validated the message, decrypts the ciphertext using "
"his own private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, si Bob, na na-validate na ang mensahe, ay dine-decrypt ang "
"ciphertext gamit ang kanyang sariling private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/dig_sig_rsa.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 2. Digital signatures with RSA*\n"
msgstr "*Figure 2. Mga digital signature gamit ang RSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This workflow for a digital signature is illustrated next.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang workflow para sa isang digital signature ay ipinapakita sa susunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We once again import some useful modules from the ``cryptography`` library.\n"
"As before, Alice intends to securely send a symmetric key to Bob, but she also wishes to digitally sign it. In this case, we need public keys for both Alice and Bob. Therefore, the first step is for both Alice and Bob to create their own key pair using RSA and broadcast their own public key to the world.\n"
msgstr ""
"Muli naming ini-import ang ilang kapaki-pakinabang na module mula sa "
"``cryptography`` library. Gaya ng dati, balak ni Alice na ligtas na "
"magpadala ng isang symmetric key kay Bob, ngunit nais din niyang digital na "
"lagdaan ito. Sa kasong ito, kailangan natin ng mga public key para sa "
"parehong si Alice at Bob. Samakatuwid, ang unang hakbang ay para sa parehong"
" si Alice at Bob na lumikha ng kanilang sariling key pair gamit ang RSA at "
"ibahagi ang kanilang sariling public key sa lahat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the next step, as before, Alice uses Bob's public key to encrypt the "
"symmetric key and prepares the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa susunod na hakbang, gaya ng dati, ginagamit ni Alice ang public key ni "
"Bob para i-encrypt ang symmetric key at inihahanda ang ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this stage, instead of just broadcasting the ciphertext, Alice intends to"
" attach a digital signature to it so that she can prove to Bob that she was "
"the sender of the message. This is done in two steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa yugtong ito, sa halip na ibahagi lamang ang ciphertext, balak ni Alice na"
" mag-attach ng digital signature dito para mapatunayan niya kay Bob na siya "
"ang nagpadala ng mensahe. Ginagawa ito sa dalawang hakbang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Create a hash of the ciphertext using a hashing algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Lumikha ng hash ng ciphertext gamit ang isang hashing algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encrypt the hash using Alice's private key, which amounts to a signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-encrypt ang hash gamit ang private key ni Alice, na katumbas ng isang "
"signature.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice then broadcasts the ciphertext and the signature over a network so "
"that Bob is able to intercept both of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinahagi ni Alice ang ciphertext at signature sa isang network para "
"matanggap ni Bob ang pareho sa kanila.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On Bob's side, the first task is to verify the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Integrity is maintained when a message is protected against "
"unauthorized change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the ciphertext. To "
"do this, Bob creates a hash of the received ciphertext using the same "
"hashing algorithm used by Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa panig ni Bob, ang unang gawain ay i-verify ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang integridad ay napanatili kapag ang isang mensahe ay "
"protektado laban sa hindi awtorisadong "
"pagbabago.\">integridad</DefinitionTooltip> at <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang pagiging tunay ay ang patunay na ang isang mensahe ay "
"nagmula sa pinagmulan na inaangkin nito.\">pagiging "
"tunay</DefinitionTooltip> ng ciphertext. Para gawin ito, gumagawa si Bob ng "
"hash ng natanggap na ciphertext gamit ang parehong hashing algorithm na "
"ginamit ni Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Bob decrypts the received signature using Alice's public key. Because "
"Alice used her private key to create the signature, Bob is able to decrypt "
"it using Alice's public key. The decrypted signature is nothing but a hash "
"of the ciphertext created on Alice's end. If the hash created by Bob matches"
" the decrypted signature, then Bob has verified that the ciphertext he "
"received has not been tampered with and that it was Alice who signed the "
"ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, dine-decrypt ni Bob ang natanggap na signature gamit ang public "
"key ni Alice. Dahil ginamit ni Alice ang kanyang private key para gumawa ng "
"signature, nagagawa ni Bob na i-decrypt ito gamit ang public key ni Alice. "
"Ang na-decrypt na signature ay wala nang iba kundi isang hash ng ciphertext "
"na ginawa sa panig ni Alice. Kung ang hash na ginawa ni Bob ay tumutugma sa "
"na-decrypt na signature, napatunayan ni Bob na ang ciphertext na natanggap "
"niya ay hindi binago at si Alice ang naglagda ng ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Python code below, these operations are combined into a useful "
"utility function called ``verify`` provided by an object associated with "
"Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa Python code sa ibaba, ang mga operasyong ito ay pinagsama sa isang "
"kapaki-pakinabang na utility function na tinatawag na ``verify`` na "
"ibinibigay ng isang object na nauugnay sa public key ni Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having verified the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Integrity is maintained "
"when a message is protected against unauthorized "
"change.\">integrity</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Authenticity is the proof that a message is from the source it "
"claims to be from.\">authenticity</DefinitionTooltip> of the received "
"ciphertext, Bob can then decrypt it using his private key because Alice "
"created the ciphertext using Bob's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos ma-verify ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Ang integridad ay "
"napanatili kapag ang isang mensahe ay protektado laban sa hindi awtorisadong"
" pagbabago.\">integridad</DefinitionTooltip> at <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang pagiging tunay ay ang patunay na ang isang mensahe ay "
"nagmula sa pinagmulan na inaangkin nito.\">pagiging "
"tunay</DefinitionTooltip> ng natanggap na ciphertext, maaari na si Bob na "
"i-decrypt ito gamit ang kanyang private key dahil nilikha ni Alice ang "
"ciphertext gamit ang public key ni Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above digital signature scenario, any party — not just Bob — can "
"verify that Alice is the sender of the ciphertext because everyone can "
"access Alice's public key, the ciphertext, and the digital signature. "
"Furthermore, after sending the ciphertext and the signature, Alice cannot "
"later deny having done so because the signature can be decrypted to a "
"meaningful hash using only her public key. This establishes "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Non-repudiation refers to the ability to "
"prove that a specific party has sent a message. In symmetric key "
"cryptography, since the same key is used for both encryption and decryption,"
" it is not possible to determine which party has created a particular "
"ciphertext. In contrast, asymmetric key cryptography provides non-"
"repudiation through the use of digital signatures.\">non-"
"repudiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sitwasyon ng digital signature sa itaas, anumang partido — hindi lamang "
"si Bob — ay makakapag-verify na si Alice ang nagpadala ng ciphertext dahil "
"maaaring ma-access ng lahat ang public key ni Alice, ang ciphertext, at ang "
"digital signature. Bukod pa rito, pagkatapos ipadala ang ciphertext at ang "
"signature, hindi na maaaring itanggi ni Alice na ginawa niya ito dahil ang "
"signature ay maaaring ma-decrypt sa isang makahulugang hash gamit ang "
"kanyang public key lamang. Itinatayo nito ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Ang non-repudiation ay tumutukoy sa kakayahang patunayan na ang"
" isang tiyak na partido ay nagpadala ng isang mensahe. Sa symmetric key "
"cryptography, dahil ang parehong key ay ginagamit para sa parehong "
"encryption at decryption, hindi posible na matukoy kung aling partido ang "
"lumikha ng isang partikular na ciphertext. Sa kabaligtaran, ang asymmetric "
"key cryptography ay nagbibigay ng non-repudiation sa pamamagitan ng paggamit"
" ng mga digital signature.\">non-repudiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By enabling secure key distribution and supporting non-repudiation, public "
"key cryptography establishes a strong foundation for secure digital "
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagpapagana ng ligtas na pamamahagi ng key at pagsuporta "
"sa non-repudiation, ang public key cryptography ay nagtatayo ng matibay na "
"pundasyon para sa ligtas na digital na komunikasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking RSA {#breaking-rsa}"
msgstr "Pagsira ng RSA {#breaking-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The utility and security of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key"
" cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm outlined above rests "
"on two mathematical assumptions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagiging kapaki-pakinabang at seguridad ng <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, "
"and Leonard Adleman. Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm "
"na nakabalangkas sa itaas ay nakasalalay sa dalawang matematikal na "
"pagpapalagay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finding the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ given "
"that access only to $(e, n)$ is computationally infeasible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang paghanap ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and "
"modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular multiplicative inverse</DefinitionTooltip> $d$ kung ang "
"tanging access lamang ay sa $(e, n)$ ay hindi magagawa sa makatwirang oras "
"ng kompyutasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the RSA setting, the modular exponentiation operation behaves like a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it is easy to "
"compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the inputs from the"
" output.\">one-way trapdoor function</DefinitionTooltip>. When used for "
"encryption, it yields ciphertext that is inscrutable, and without access to "
"the private key, inverting the operation to recover the plain text from the "
"ciphertext is not feasible. However, with access to the private key, which "
"acts as a trapdoor, the ciphertext can be easily decrypted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa konteksto ng RSA, ang operasyon ng modular exponentiation ay kumikilos "
"tulad ng isang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A one-way function where it "
"is easy to compute an output from the inputs, but hard to determine the "
"inputs from the output.\">one-way trapdoor function</DefinitionTooltip>. "
"Kapag ginamit para sa encryption, nagbubunga ito ng ciphertext na hindi "
"mababasa, at nang wala ang access sa private key, ang pag-invert ng "
"operasyon para mabawi ang plain text mula sa ciphertext ay hindi magagawa. "
"Gayunpaman, kapag may access sa private key na gumaganap bilang trapdoor, "
"madaling ma-decrypt ang ciphertext.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most prominent attack on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-"
"key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm aims to undermine "
"assumption 1 by efficiently recovering the private key number $d$ via "
"factorizing the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The modulus is the remainder"
" left over after dividing by the value specified. modulo is the operation of"
" doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. As will be illustrated "
"below, it is easy to recover $d$ if one has access to either the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"prime factors of a number n, are those "
"primes that are multiplied together to make n.\">prime "
"factors</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ and $q$ of $n$ or the totient "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used to "
"indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$. Recall that $p$, "
"$q$, and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, phi, often used "
"to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ are kept secret "
"during key generation and discarded after. A third party that recovers this "
"information using a classical or quantum computer essentially uncovers the "
"private key, breaking RSA. Thus, prime factorization is the key "
"computational primitive necessary for breaking RSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinaka-kilalang pag-atake sa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-"
"key cryptosystem named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. "
"Developed in 1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip> algorithm ay naglalayong sirain"
" ang pagpapalagay 1 sa pamamagitan ng mahusay na pagbawi ng private key "
"number $d$ sa pamamagitan ng factorization ng <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the "
"value specified. modulo is the operation of doing "
"this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$. Tulad ng mailalatag sa ibaba, "
"madaling mabawi ang $d$ kung may access ang isa sa <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"prime factors of a number n, are those primes that are "
"multiplied together to make n.\">prime factors</DefinitionTooltip> $p$ at "
"$q$ ng $n$ o sa totient <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek symbol, "
"phi, often used to indicate Euler's totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$."
" Alalahanin na ang $p$, $q$, at <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The greek "
"symbol, phi, often used to indicate Euler's "
"totient.\">$φ$</DefinitionTooltip>$(n)$ ay pinananatiling lihim sa panahon "
"ng key generation at tinatanggal pagkatapos. Ang isang third party na "
"nakakabawi ng impormasyong ito gamit ang isang klasikal o quantum na "
"kompyuter ay mahalagang natuklasan ang private key, na sinisira ang RSA. "
"Kaya naman, ang prime factorization ang pangunahing computational primitive "
"na kailangan para sirain ang RSA.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Classical computing and RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Klasikal na computing at RSA {#classical-computing-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prime factorization of large integers is known to exhibit <DefinitionTooltip"
" definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial</DefinitionTooltip> or <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For example polynomial and "
"linear scaling.\">subexponential</DefinitionTooltip> scaling on classical "
"computers. The best-known classical algorithm for factoring integers larger "
"than $10^{100}$ is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field "
"Sieve - An efficient classical algorithm for factoring large "
"integers.\">*general number field sieve*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang prime factorization ng malalaking integer ay kilala na nagpapakita ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for "
"example, an exponential function.\">super-polynomial</DefinitionTooltip> o "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scaling slower than exponential. For example"
" polynomial and linear scaling.\">subexponential</DefinitionTooltip> na "
"scaling sa mga klasikal na kompyuter. Ang pinaka-kilalang klasikal na "
"algorithm para sa factoring ng mga integer na mas malaki sa $10^{100}$ ay "
"ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An "
"efficient classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">*general "
"number field sieve*</DefinitionTooltip> "
"[(GNFS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=General_number_field_sieve&oldid=1151781536)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: <Accordion>
# <AccordionItem title="Matematikal na detalye">
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "as a function of the integer $n$ to be factorized.\n"
msgstr ""
"$L_n[\\frac{1}{3}, (\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})}] = "
"e^{[((\\frac{64}{9})^{(\\frac{1}{3})} + o(1)) "
"(log(n))^{\\frac{1}{3}}(log(log(n))^{\\frac{2}{3}})]}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This scaling is super-polynomial in the number of bits required to represent"
" $n$.\n"
msgstr "bilang function ng integer $n$ na ifa-factor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, prime factorization is considered inefficient on classical "
"computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang scaling na ito ay super-polynomial sa bilang ng mga bit na kailangan "
"para katawanin ang $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Samakatuwid, ang
# prime factorization ay itinuturing na hindi
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: </AccordionItem>
# </Accordion>
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At present, the [largest integers factored on classical "
"hardware](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_Factoring_Challenge&oldid=1163481797)"
" are in the range of 829 bits or 250 decimal digits. Given the exponential "
"growth in classical computing power that has been witnessed over the last "
"several decades, 1024-bit RSA is no longer considered secure in the near "
"term and is now deprecated. Nevertheless, in the foreseeable future, "
"factoring 2048-bit integers whose magnitude are in the range of $10^{617}$ "
"is at present considered infeasible on classical systems, suggesting "
"continued viability. The advent of quantum computers, however, voids this "
"assessment.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shor's quantum algorithm and RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"
msgstr "Shor's quantum algorithm at RSA {#shors-quantum-algorithm-and-rsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: dropped, JSX/HTML tags differ from English: Ang Shor's
# algorithm ay maaaring mag-factor ng mga prime gam
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Probably the most well-known quantum algorithm today is <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. "
"Developed by the mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for finding the prime factors of integers. "
"When [introduced by Peter Shor in "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), it was recognized as the "
"first quantum algorithm that offered a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial; for example, an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> relative to "
"classical algorithms on a problem of great practical importance, namely "
"prime factorization.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm can factor primes with $O(n^2)$ where $n$ is the number of bits.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical explanation of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na paliwanag ng Shor's algorithm\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem "
"named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Developed in "
"1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip>, <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. Developed by the "
"mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"works by exploiting the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at "
"which a function repeats itself.\">periodicity</DefinitionTooltip> of the "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when"
" an integer is raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number "
"(modulus). For example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponential "
"function</DefinitionTooltip> $f(x) = a^x (mod~n)$ and provides a quantum "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding primitive that enables "
"efficient prime factorization of the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa konteksto ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A public-key cryptosystem "
"named after Ron Rivest, Adi Shamir, and Leonard Adleman. Developed in "
"1977.\">RSA</DefinitionTooltip>, ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"quantum algorithm which can find prime factors efficiently. Developed by the"
" mathematician, Peter Shor, in 1994.\">Shor's algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"ay gumagana sa pamamagitan ng pagsasamantala sa <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">periodicity</DefinitionTooltip> ng <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponential function</DefinitionTooltip> "
"$f(x) = a^x (mod~n)$ at nagbibigay ng quantum <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding primitive na nagbibigay-daan sa"
" mahusay na prime factorization ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"modulus is the remainder left over after dividing by the value specified. "
"modulo is the operation of doing this.\">modulus</DefinitionTooltip> $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simplified high-level outline of Shor's overall scheme for breaking RSA is"
" as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang simplified na mataas na antas na balangkas ng pangkalahatang "
"scheme ni Shor para sa pagsira ng RSA ay ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the modulus $n$, which is published as part of the public key, choose "
"a number $a$ coprime to $n$ that is, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. Since we know that $n ="
" p*q$ has exactly two prime factors $(p, q)$, almost any number less than "
"$n$ that we pick at random is likely to be coprime to $n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil sa modulus $n$, na inilathala bilang bahagi ng public key, pumili ng "
"isang numero $a$ na coprime sa $n$, ibig sabihin, $gcd(a,n) = 1$. Dahil alam"
" natin na ang $n = p*q$ ay may eksaktong dalawang prime factor $(p, q)$, "
"halos kahit anong numero na mas mababa sa $n$ na ating napili nang random ay"
" malamang na coprime sa $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Having chosen $a$, find the exponent $r$ such that $a^r \\equiv 1 (mod~n)$. "
"This implies $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. The existence of an "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a number is multiplied "
"by itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ such that the above "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence ie. all behaving"
" in the same way.\">congruence</DefinitionTooltip> holds is guaranteed by "
"the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats"
" itself.\">periodicity property</DefinitionTooltip> of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when an integer is "
"raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number (modulus). For "
"example $x^e mod m$.\">modular exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos mapili ang $a$, hanapin ang exponent $r$ na $a^r \\equiv 1 "
"(mod~n)$. Ipinahihiwatig nito na $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n)$. Ang "
"pagkakaroon ng isang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The number of times a "
"number is multiplied by itself.\">exponent</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ na "
"natutugunan ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Consistency, or equivalence "
"ie. all behaving in the same way.\">congruence</DefinitionTooltip> sa itaas "
"ay ginagarantiyahan ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which"
" a function repeats itself.\">periodicity property</DefinitionTooltip> ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Modular exponentiation is the remainder when"
" an integer is raised to a power (exponent) and then divided by a number "
"(modulus). For example $x^e mod m$.\">modular "
"exponentiation</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $r$ is even, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) (a^{r/2} "
"+ 1) =  \\gamma*n$ for some integer $\\gamma$. The left-hand side of this "
"latter equality must contain $p$ and $q$ as two of its prime factors since "
"the right-hand side does. If $r$ is odd, go back to step 1 and try a "
"different choice for $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang $r$ ay pantay, $a^r - 1 \\equiv 0 (mod~n) \\implies (a^{r/2} - 1) "
"(a^{r/2} + 1) =  \\gamma*n$ para sa ilang integer $\\gamma$. Ang kaliwang "
"bahagi ng huli na pagkakatumbas na ito ay dapat naglalaman ng $p$ at $q$ "
"bilang dalawa sa mga prime factor nito dahil ganoon ang kanang bahagi. Kung "
"ang $r$ ay gansal (odd), bumalik sa hakbang 1 at subukan ang ibang "
"pagpipilian para sa $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating the "
"greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the original "
"Euclidean algorithm.\">extended Euclid algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> for "
"finding $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ or $gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. The computed "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest "
"positive whole number that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip>is very likely to identify one of the "
"prime factors $p$ or $q$. Divide $n$ with this prime factor to recover the "
"other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An efficient way of calculating "
"the greatest common divisor of two whole numbers. It improves on the "
"original Euclidean algorithm.\">extended Euclid "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip> para sa paghanap ng $gcd((a^{r/2} - 1), n)$ o "
"$gcd((a^{r/2} + 1), n)$. Ang kinakalkula na <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor - the largest positive whole number "
"that can divide two or more of the given whole "
"numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> ay malamang na makilala ang isa sa mga "
"prime factor $p$ o $q$. Hatiin ang $n$ gamit ang prime factor na ito para "
"mabawi ang isa pa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once $p, q$ are known, use the steps from the original RSA algorithm for "
"reconstructing the totient $\\phi(n)$ and generating the private key number "
"$d$ as the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, and modulus"
" $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the known public key "
"number $e$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nakilala na ang $p, q$, gamitin ang mga hakbang mula sa orihinal na "
"RSA algorithm para muling buuin ang totient $\\phi(n)$ at buuin ang private "
"key number $d$ bilang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$, "
"and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> ng kilalang public key "
"number $e$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In August 2023 Oded Regev [published an improvement](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.06572) on Shor's original using a multi-dimensional approach resulting in $O(n^{1.5})$. There continues to be further research including by [Ragavan and Vaikuntanathan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.00899) in this area which may improve time, cost, or number of qubits needed. Whilst we cannot say when running such algorithms against real-world RSA encryption truly becomes viable, it is becoming closer all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Noong Agosto 2023, nag-[publish si Oded Regev ng isang pagpapabuti](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2308.06572) sa orihinal ni Shor gamit ang isang multi-dimensional na diskarte na nagresulta sa $O(n^{1.5})$. Patuloy pa rin ang karagdagang pananaliksik kabilang na ang ginagawa nina [Ragavan at Vaikuntanathan](https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2310.00899) sa larangang ito na maaaring magpabuti ng oras, gastos, o bilang ng mga qubit na kailangan. Bagama't hindi natin masasabi kung kailan talagang magiging viable ang pagpapatakbo ng ganitong mga algorithm laban sa tunay na RSA encryption, lalo itong naglalapitan sa atin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Python example demonstrating breaking RSA encryption {#python-example-"
"demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa sa Python na nagpapakita ng pagsira ng RSA encryption {#python-"
"example-demonstrating-breaking-rsa-encryption}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following code cells, we illustrate an example of finding a private "
"key given only the public key. This will use brute-force classical "
"computation, but shows how Shor's algorithm could be used - including large "
"keys.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga sumusunod na code cell, naglarawan tayo ng halimbawa ng paghanap ng "
"isang private key habang binibigyan lamang ng public key. Gagamitin nito ang"
" brute-force na klasikal na kompyutasyon, ngunit ipinapakita kung paano "
"maaaring gamitin ang Shor's algorithm — kabilang ang malalaking key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"In this section we will show the math calculations in detail as part of the Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Sa seksyong ito, ipapakita natin ang mga matematikal na kalkulasyon nang detalyado bilang bahagi ng Python code\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the example, we have a public key $(5, 247)$, and we will recover the "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halimbawa, mayroon tayong public key $(5, 247)$, at mabawi natin ang "
"private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** The first step is to pick a number coprime to 247. Almost any "
"number we guess will do the job. Let's pick 6.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 1:** Ang unang hakbang ay pumili ng isang numero na coprime sa "
"247. Halos kahit anong numero na ating hulaan ay gagawin ang trabaho. Pumili"
" tayo ng 6.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 2:** Next we need to find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The "
"interval at which a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> "
"$r$ such that $6^r \\equiv 1 (mod~247)$. In this example, we compute $r$ "
"classically using brute force, but we could also use Shor's algorithm on a "
"quantum computer using <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK "
"for working with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 2:** Susunod, kailangan nating hanapin ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> $r$ na $6^r \\equiv 1 (mod~247)$. Sa "
"halimbawang ito, kinakalkula natin ang $r$ nang klasikal gamit ang brute "
"force, ngunit maaari rin tayong gumamit ng Shor's algorithm sa isang quantum"
" na kompyuter gamit ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An open-source SDK "
"for working with quantum algorithms and computers. Developed by "
"IBM.\">Qiskit</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 3:** Since the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which "
"a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ is even, we"
" can compute $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 3:** Dahil ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at "
"which a function repeats itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip> $r = 36$ ay "
"pantay, maaari tayong mag-compute ng $f1 = (a^{r/2}-1), f2=(a^{r/2}+1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** Find the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common Divisor"
" - the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of the "
"given whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> of either of those factors "
"with $n$. Simply divide $n$ with the prime factor already found to obtain "
"the second prime factor.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 4:** Hanapin ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Greatest Common "
"Divisor - the largest positive whole number that can divide two or more of "
"the given whole numbers.\">GCD</DefinitionTooltip> ng alinman sa mga factor "
"na iyon gamit ang $n$. Hatiin lamang ang $n$ gamit ang prime factor na "
"nahanap na para makuha ang pangalawang prime factor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 5:** Having recovered the prime factors of $n = 247$ as "
"$p_{found}=13$ and $q_{found}=19$, we compute the totient $\\phi_{found} = "
"(p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 5:** Pagkatapos mabawi ang mga prime factor ng $n = 247$ bilang "
"$p_{found}=13$ at $q_{found}=19$, kinakalkula natin ang totient "
"$\\phi_{found} = (p_{found}-1)*(q_{found}-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$,"
" and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> of the public key number "
"$e=5$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang private key ay ang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Given an integer $a$,"
" and modulus $m$, the remainder from ax/m is 1. This is only the case for "
"coprimes.\">modular inverse</DefinitionTooltip> ng public key number "
"$e=5$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above scheme, step 2 is the crucial <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding operation for which [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" uses two fundamental quantum primitives, namely the <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*quantum Fourier "
"transform*</DefinitionTooltip> and <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum"
" algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in"
" classical physics.\">*quantum phase estimation*</DefinitionTooltip>. For a "
"detailed explanation of the quantum aspects of Shor's algorithm, see the "
"Phase estimation and factoring lesson in the [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Steps 1 "
"and 3 through 5 involve relatively inexpensive operations that can be easily"
" carried out on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa scheme sa itaas, ang hakbang 2 ang mahalagang operasyon ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The interval at which a function repeats "
"itself.\">period</DefinitionTooltip>-finding kung saan ginagamit ng [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Shor%27s_algorithm&oldid=1164409434)"
" ang dalawang pangunahing quantum primitive, lalo na ang <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns."
" Named after the fourier transform in classical physics which can split a "
"signal into a set of sine waves.\">*quantum Fourier "
"transform*</DefinitionTooltip> at <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum "
"algorithm used to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in "
"classical physics.\">*quantum phase estimation*</DefinitionTooltip>. Para sa"
" detalyadong paliwanag ng mga quantum aspeto ng Shor's algorithm, tingnan "
"ang aralin na Phase estimation and factoring sa [Fundamentals of Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms). Ang mga "
"hakbang 1 at 3 hanggang 5 ay nagsasangkot ng mga operasyong medyo hindi "
"mahal na madaling maisagawa sa mga klasikal na kompyuter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, here's a detailed visual walkthrough of implementing [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"
msgstr ""
"Opsyonal, narito ang isang detalyadong visual na walkthrough ng pagpapatupad"
" ng [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EdJ7RoWcU48&t=325s).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On quantum computers, Shor's algorithm can exhibit <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to logarithmic scaling, that "
"is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A binary search is a simple "
"example.\">polylogarithmic scaling</DefinitionTooltip> as favorable as "
"$O((log~n)^2 (log~log~n))$ in terms of the modulus $n$, or "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scales relative to a power, for example n^3."
" Grows quicker than linear scaling, but slower than "
"exponential.\">polynomial scaling</DefinitionTooltip> in terms of the number"
" of bits needed to represent $n$. This is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial, for example an exponential "
"function.\">super-polynomial speedup</DefinitionTooltip> compared to the "
"classical <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An "
"efficient classical algorithm for factoring large integers.\">GNFS "
"algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga quantum na kompyuter, ang Shor's algorithm ay maaaring magpakita ng "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"An algorithm which scales similar to "
"logarithmic scaling, that is, efficiently compared to the size of data. A "
"binary search is a simple example.\">polylogarithmic "
"scaling</DefinitionTooltip> na kasingabuti ng $O((log~n)^2 (log~log~n))$ sa "
"mga tuntunin ng modulus $n$, o <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Scales "
"relative to a power, for example n^3. Grows quicker than linear scaling, but"
" slower than exponential.\">polynomial scaling</DefinitionTooltip> sa mga "
"tuntunin ng bilang ng mga bit na kailangan para katawanin ang $n$. Ito ay "
"isang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Growing faster than a polynomial, for "
"example an exponential function.\">super-polynomial na "
"speedup</DefinitionTooltip> kumpara sa klasikal na <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"General Number Field Sieve - An efficient classical algorithm "
"for factoring large integers.\">GNFS algorithm</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Recent resource estimates](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) indicate that based on certain "
"assumptions made regarding the hardware configuration, a few tens of "
"thousands to several million <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum bit, "
"the equivalent of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves very "
"differently since it can be in superposition, (imagine a combination of "
"states), but once measured the superposition collapses, and the result will "
"be 0 or 1.\">qubits</DefinitionTooltip> will be necessary to break 2048-bit "
"RSA using Shor's algorithm. It is not inconceivable that quantum computers "
"with several tens of thousands of qubits will become available over the next"
" several years, making the lower end of the resource estimate accessible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [mga kamakailang tantya ng resources](https://quantum-"
"journal.org/papers/q-2021-04-15-433/) ay nagpapahiwatig na batay sa ilang "
"mga pagpapalagay na ginawa tungkol sa configuration ng hardware, ilang "
"sampung libo hanggang ilang milyong <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"quantum bit, the equivalent of a bit in classical computing. A qubit behaves"
" very differently since it can be in superposition, (imagine a combination "
"of states), but once measured the superposition collapses, and the result "
"will be 0 or 1.\">qubit</DefinitionTooltip> ang kailangan para sirain ang "
"2048-bit RSA gamit ang Shor's algorithm. Hindi imposible na ang mga quantum "
"na kompyuter na may ilang sampung libong qubit ay magiging available sa "
"susunod na ilang taon, na ginagawang accessible ang pinakamababang dulo ng "
"tantya ng resources.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diffie-Hellman key exchange and the Digital Signature Algorithm {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"
msgstr ""
"Diffie-Hellman key exchange at ang Digital Signature Algorithm {#diffie-"
"hellman-key-exchange-and-the-digital-signature-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous section, we discussed the RSA cryptosystem, whose security "
"is based on the computational hardness of prime factorization. Here, we will"
" discuss two popular asymmetric key cryptographic protocols, [*Diffie-"
"Hellman* key "
"exchange](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and the [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), both of which are based on a different mathematical problem, namely "
"the discrete logarithm problem (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang seksyon, tinalakay natin ang RSA cryptosystem, na ang seguridad"
" ay batay sa computational na kahirapan ng prime factorization. Dito, "
"tatalakayin natin ang dalawang sikat na asymmetric key cryptographic "
"protocol, ang [*Diffie-Hellman* key "
"exchange](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) at ang [*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), na parehong batay sa ibang matematikal na problema, lalo na ang "
"discrete logarithm problem (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The discrete logarithm problem {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr "Ang discrete logarithm problem {#the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In the following equation we need to find $a$ given only $e$,$M$,$c$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sumusunod na equation kailangan nating hanapin ang $a$ dahil sa $e$, $M$,"
" $c$ lamang\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"
msgstr "$a^e$ $mod$ $M = c$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is believed to be difficult with classic computers due to the use of "
"modulo arithmetic, and therefore is a good mathematical basis for an "
"encryption algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay pinaniniwalaan na mahirap sa mga klasikal na kompyuter dahil sa "
"paggamit ng modulo arithmetic, at samakatuwid ay isang magandang matematikal"
" na pundasyon para sa isang encryption algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is known as the [discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay kilala bilang ang [discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Discrete_logarithm&oldid=1161792952)"
" (DLP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mathematical details of the discrete logarithm problem {#mathematical-"
"details-of-the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Matematikal na detalye ng discrete logarithm problem {#mathematical-details-"
"of-the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DLP is typically framed in the context of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Group where all elements are generated by repeatedly applying a"
" single element, known as a generator. This process creates a cycle of "
"elements that closes upon itself.\">cyclic groups</DefinitionTooltip> and is"
" stated as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang DLP ay karaniwang nakabalangkas sa konteksto ng mga <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Group where all elements are generated by repeatedly applying a"
" single element, known as a generator. This process creates a cycle of "
"elements that closes upon itself.\">cyclic group</DefinitionTooltip> at "
"isinasaad tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider a [cyclic "
"group](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ generated by a group element $g \\in G$ and given an arbitrary element "
"$h \\in G$, find an integer $k$ such that $h = g^{k}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang isang [cyclic "
"group](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Cyclic_group&oldid=1150017831)"
" $G$ na nabuo ng isang group element $g \\in G$ at dahil sa isang arbitrary "
"na elemento $h \\in G$, hanapin ang isang integer $k$ na $h = g^{k}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here the integer $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ is the discrete logarithm. The cyclic "
"property of $G$ guarantees that for every $h$, a valid integer $k$ exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ang integer $k \\equiv log_{g}h$ ay ang discrete logarithm. Ang cyclic "
"property ng $G$ ay ginagarantiyahan na para sa bawat $h$, may valid na "
"integer $k$ na umiiral.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For cryptography, the DLP on the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The set of "
"integers modulo a prime number, where the group operation is modular "
"multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group are chosen in such a "
"way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that each element has a "
"unique multiplicative inverse within the group.\">multiplicative "
"group</DefinitionTooltip> of integers modulo a prime number $p$ denoted "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ turns out to be useful. The elements of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ are congruence classes labeled by integers "
"modulo $p$ that are coprime to $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa cryptography, ang DLP sa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The set of "
"integers modulo a prime number, where the group operation is modular "
"multiplication. Elements in the multiplicative group are chosen in such a "
"way that they are coprime to the modulus, ensuring that each element has a "
"unique multiplicative inverse within the group.\">multiplicative "
"group</DefinitionTooltip> ng mga integer modulo ang isang prime number $p$ "
"na tinutukoy bilang $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ay nagpapatunay na kapaki-"
"pakinabang. Ang mga elemento ng $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ay mga "
"congruence class na may label ng mga integer modulo $p$ na coprime sa $p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For example:\n"
msgstr "Halimbawa:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"
msgstr ""
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_5)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4]\\}~\\mathrm{and}~(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} = "
"\\{[1],[2],[3],[4],[5],[6]\\} $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of multiplication $(\\times)$ on these groups is simply "
"ordinary integer multiplication followed by reduction modulo $p$ and "
"exponentiation by an integer $k$ is just repeated multiplication $k$ times "
"and reduction modulo $p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyon ng multiplication $(\\times)$ sa mga group na ito ay simpleng "
"ordinaryong integer multiplication na sinusundan ng reduction modulo $p$ at "
"ang exponentiation ng isang integer $k$ ay paulit-ulit na multiplication ng "
"$k$ na beses at reduction modulo $p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let's illustrate an instance of the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr "Ilarawan natin ang isang instance ng DLP sa $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This multiplicative group has two generators ${[3],[5]}$ also known as "
"primitive roots. We will use $[5]$ as the generator; that is, generate every"
" element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ using successive integer powers of "
"5.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang multiplicative group na ito ay may dalawang generator na ${[3],[5]}$ na "
"kilala rin bilang primitive roots. Gagamitin natin ang $[5]$ bilang "
"generator; iyon ay, bubuuin ang bawat elemento ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ gamit ang magkakasunod na integer powers ng 5.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that in modulo 7 arithmetic, raising 5 to successive integer powers "
"yields every element of $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ exactly once before the "
"cycle repeats indefinitely with a period $p-1 =6$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakita natin na sa modulo 7 arithmetic, ang pagdadala ng 5 sa magkakasunod "
"na integer powers ay nagbubunga ng bawat elemento ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ nang eksakto isang beses bago paulit-ulit ang "
"cycle nang walang katiyakan na may period na $p-1 =6$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So the DLP on $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ with generator [5] is:\n"
msgstr "Kaya ang DLP sa $(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ na may generator [5] ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$ \\mathrm{Given}~h \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times} \\mathrm{, find~} k "
"\\mathrm{~such~that~} 5^{k} \\equiv h~(mod~7)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From the above Python cell output we see that:\n"
msgstr "Mula sa output ng Python cell sa itaas, nakita natin na:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 2 \\implies k=4 \\mathrm{~or~}  4 = log_5(2) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"
msgstr "$h = 6 \\implies k=3 \\mathrm{~or~}  3 = log_5(6) (mod~7)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In ordinary real number arithmetic, exponentiation is a <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"A behavior or relationship that consistently moves in a single "
"direction without reversals; for example in a monotonically increasing "
"function, values consistently increase.\">monotonic</DefinitionTooltip> "
"function and finding the logarithm of any number to any base is "
"computationally easy. In contrast, as is apparent from the simple "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ example above, modular exponentiation is non-"
"monotonic, and even though it is periodic with period $p-1$, it is otherwise"
" highly nontrivial. So computing its inverse, the discrete logarithm turns "
"out to be inefficient for large $p$ on classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa ordinaryong real number arithmetic, ang exponentiation ay isang "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A behavior or relationship that consistently"
" moves in a single direction without reversals; for example in a "
"monotonically increasing function, values consistently "
"increase.\">monotonic</DefinitionTooltip> na function at ang paghanap ng "
"logarithm ng anumang numero sa anumang base ay madaling kalkulahin. Sa "
"kaibahan, tulad ng malinaw mula sa simpleng halimbawa ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_7)^{\\times}$ sa itaas, ang modular exponentiation ay hindi-"
"monotonic, at kahit na ito ay periodic na may period na $p-1$, ito ay "
"lubhang hindi trivial. Kaya ang pagkalkula ng inverse nito, ang discrete "
"logarithm, ay lumalabas na hindi mahusay para sa malaking $p$ sa mga "
"klasikal na kompyuter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This observation underpins both Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the "
"Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA), which are discussed in the next "
"section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang obserbasyon na ito ang nagsisilbing pundasyon ng parehong Diffie-Hellman"
" (DH) key exchange at ng Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA), na tatalakayin "
"sa susunod na seksyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The DLP can be extended to cyclic subgroups as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang DLP ay maaaring palawakin sa mga cyclic subgroup tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ defined above and an element $g \\in "
"(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order $r$ that is, $g^r \\equiv 1 "
"(~mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ na tinukoy sa itaas at isang "
"elemento $g \\in (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ng prime order $r$ iyon ay, $g^r"
" \\equiv 1 (~mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The set of integer powers of $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le r\\} = "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ is a cyclic subgroup of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ "
"with group order $r$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang hanay ng mga integer power ng $g$: $\\{g^k~(mod~p) | 1 \\le k \\le r\\} "
"= \\langle g \\rangle$ ay isang cyclic subgroup ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ na may group order $r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '-   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A DLP can be specified on $\\langle g \\rangle$ by choosing a $h \\in "
"\\langle g \\rangle$ and asking for $1 \\le a \\le r$ such that $ "
"g^a~(mod~p) = h$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang DLP ay maaaring tukuyin sa $\\langle g \\rangle$ sa pamamagitan ng"
" pagpili ng $h \\in \\langle g \\rangle$ at pagtatanong para sa $1 \\le a "
"\\le r$ na $g^a~(mod~p) = h$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"
msgstr "Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#diffie-hellman-key-exchange}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In 1976, [Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman proposed a key exchange "
"protocol](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) to enable the creation "
"of a shared secret key over insecure communication channels. The secret key "
"could then be used by parties sharing it for symmetric encryption. The "
"algorithm relies on the DLP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Noong 1976, [iminungkahi nina Whitfield Diffie at Martin Hellman ang isang "
"key exchange protocol](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055638) para "
"paganahin ang paglikha ng isang shared secret key sa mga hindi secure na "
"communication channel. Ang secret key ay maaaring magamit ng mga partido na "
"nagbabahagi nito para sa symmetric encryption. Ang algorithm ay umaasa sa "
"DLP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/key_exchange_dh.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange*\n"
msgstr "*Figure 1. Diffie-Hellman key exchange*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<Accordion>\n"
msgstr "<Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Diffie-Hellman key "
"exchange\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na detalye ng Diffie-Hellman key "
"exchange\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With Alice and Bob being the two parties communicating, the protocol works "
"as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung si Alice at Bob ang dalawang partido na nagkokomunika, ang protocol ay "
"gumagana tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a large prime number $p$ and a primitive root "
"or generator $a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, sumasang-ayon sina Alice at Bob sa isang malaking prime number $p$ at "
"isang primitive root o generator $a$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ randomly with $1 \\le k_A \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. $k_A, h_A$ are Alice's  private"
" and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, pumipili si Alice ng isang lihim na exponent $k_A$ nang random "
"na may $1 \\le k_A \\le p-2$ at kinakalkula ang $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Ang"
" $k_A, h_A$ ay ang private at public key ni Alice ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ randomly with  $1 \\le k_B \\le "
"p-2$ and calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. $k_B, h_B$ are Bob's  private "
"and public keys respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, pumipili si Bob ng isang lihim na exponent $k_B$ nang random na may"
" $1 \\le k_B \\le p-2$ at kinakalkula ang $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$. Ang $k_B,"
" h_B$ ay ang private at public key ni Bob ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice sends Bob $h_A$ and Bob sends Alice $h_B$ over a reliable but "
"not necessarily secure channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, nagpadala si Alice kay Bob ng $h_A$ at nagpadala si Bob kay "
"Alice ng $h_B$ sa isang maaasahan ngunit hindi necessarily secure na "
"channel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, Alice then uses the $h_B$ she received to compute the shared secret "
"key $ \\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, ginagamit ni Alice ang $h_B$ na natanggap niya para kalkulahin "
"ang shared secret key na $\\kappa = h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob meanwhile uses the $h_A$ he received to compute the shared "
"secret key $ \\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, samantala ginagamit ni Bob ang $h_A$ na natanggap niya para "
"kalkulahin ang shared secret key na $\\kappa = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "With this protocol,\n"
msgstr "Sa protocol na ito,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob are guaranteed to end up with the same secret key $\\kappa$ "
"because $h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A k_B}~(mod~p) ="
" (a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"
msgstr ""
"Garantisadong matatapos sina Alice at Bob na may parehong secret key "
"$\\kappa$ dahil ang $h_B^{k_A}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_B})^{k_A}~(mod~p) = a^{k_A "
"k_B}~(mod~p) = (a^{k_A})^{k_B}~(mod~p) = h_A^{k_B}~(mod~p) $.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A third party that intercepts $h_A$ or $h_B$ cannot construct the secret key"
" $\\kappa$ because they do not have access to $k_B$ or $k_A$ respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang third party na humarang sa $h_A$ o $h_B$ ay hindi makakagawa ng "
"secret key $\\kappa$ dahil wala silang access sa $k_B$ o $k_A$ ayon sa "
"pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Extracting $k_A$ or $k_B$ using the public information $a$, $p$, $h_A$ and "
"$h_B$ is computationally hard as it is equivalent to solving the DLP on "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagkuha ng $k_A$ o $k_B$ gamit ang pampublikong impormasyon na $a$, $p$,"
" $h_A$ at $h_B$ ay computationally mahirap dahil ito ay katumbas ng paglutas"
" ng DLP sa $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of the Diffie-Hellman protocol in Python {#illustration-of-the-"
"diffie-hellman-protocol-in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Ilustrasyon ng Diffie-Hellman protocol sa Python {#illustration-of-the-"
"diffie-hellman-protocol-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's look at a simple example of the DH protocol in Python using small "
"prime numbers:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan natin ang isang simpleng halimbawa ng DH protocol sa Python gamit "
"ang maliliit na prime number:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 1:** Alice and Bob agree on a prime $p$ and a primitive root $a$. "
"Let's choose $p=11, a=7$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 1:** Sumasang-ayon sina Alice at Bob sa isang prime $p$ at isang "
"primitive root $a$. Pumili tayo ng $p=11, a=7$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 2, 3:** Alice chooses a secret exponent $k_A$ and calculates $h_A = "
"a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Similarly, Bob chooses a secret exponent $k_B$ and "
"calculates $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga Hakbang 2, 3:** Pumipili si Alice ng lihim na exponent $k_A$ at "
"kinakalkula ang $h_A = a^{k_A}~(mod~p)$. Katulad nito, pumipili si Bob ng "
"lihim na exponent $k_B$ at kinakalkula ang $h_B = a^{k_B}~(mod~p)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Step 4:** The two parties broadcast their public keys $h_A$ and $h_B$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Hakbang 4:** Ini-broadcast ng dalawang partido ang kanilang mga public key"
" na $h_A$ at $h_B$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Steps 5, 6:** Each party combines their private key with the other party's"
" public key to create the shared secret key.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga Hakbang 5, 6:** Pinagsasama ng bawat partido ang kanilang private key "
"sa public key ng kabilang partido para likhain ang shared secret key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can now use the shared secret key for symmetric encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na ngayong gamitin nina Alice at Bob ang shared secret key para sa "
"symmetric encryption.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Security of Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#security-of-diffie-hellman-key-"
"exchange}"
msgstr ""
"Seguridad ng Diffie-Hellman key exchange {#security-of-diffie-hellman-key-"
"exchange}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As noted above, the security of DH is predicated on the computational "
"difficulty of solving the DLP with large primes $p$. In typical "
"applications, NIST recommends 2048- or 3072-bit prime integers for DH key "
"exchange, which is considered sufficiently secure against attempts to solve "
"the DLP using classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng nabanggit sa itaas, ang seguridad ng DH ay nakabatay sa "
"computational na kahirapan ng paglutas ng DLP gamit ang malalaking prime "
"$p$. Sa karaniwang mga aplikasyon, inirerekomenda ng NIST ang 2048- o "
"3072-bit na prime integer para sa DH key exchange, na itinuturing na sapat "
"na secure laban sa mga pagtatangkang lutasin ang DLP gamit ang mga klasikal "
"na kompyuter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Man-in-the-middle (MITM) attacks**: The fact that DH is an interactive "
"scheme where the shared secret depends on combining one party's private key "
"with the other party's public key makes it vulnerable to a so-called *Man-"
"in-the-middle (MITM)* attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga pag-atake ng Man-in-the-middle (MITM)**: Ang katotohanan na ang DH ay "
"isang interactive na scheme kung saan ang shared secret ay nakasalalay sa "
"pagsasama ng private key ng isang partido sa public key ng kabilang partido "
"ay ginagawa itong mahina laban sa tinatawag na *Man-in-the-middle (MITM)* na"
" pag-atake.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DH security and MITM "
"attacks\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na detalye ng seguridad ng DH at mga pag-"
"atake ng MITM\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this scenario, a third party — say, Eve — intercepts the public keys "
"$h_A, h_B$ during transmission and substitutes her own public key $h_E$ for "
"each of $h_A$ and $h_B$ before forwarding them along to Bob and Alice, "
"respectively.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa sitwasyong ito, ang isang third party — sabihin nating si Eve — ay "
"humarang sa mga public key na $h_A, h_B$ sa panahon ng pagpapadala at "
"pinapalitan ang kanyang sariling public key na $h_E$ para sa bawat isa sa "
"$h_A$ at $h_B$ bago ipadala ang mga ito sa Bob at Alice ayon sa "
"pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Then, instead of using $h_B$ to create her shared secret, Alice will use "
"$h_E$ while thinking that she is using Bob's public key. Similarly, instead "
"of using $h_A$ to create his shared secret, Bob will use $h_E$ while "
"thinking that he is using Alice's public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, sa halip na gamitin ang $h_B$ para likhain ang kanyang shared "
"secret, gagamitin ni Alice ang $h_E$ habang iniisip niya na ginagamit niya "
"ang public key ni Bob. Katulad nito, sa halip na gamitin ang $h_A$ para "
"likhain ang kanyang shared secret, gagamitin ni Bob ang $h_E$ habang iniisip"
" niya na ginagamit niya ang public key ni Alice.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $h_E$ was used to create Alice's (Bob's) shared secret, plain text "
"encrypted by Alice (Bob) can be decrypted by Eve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang $h_E$ ay ginamit para likhain ang shared secret ni Alice (ni Bob),"
" ang plain text na naka-encrypt ni Alice (ni Bob) ay maaaring ma-decrypt ni "
"Eve.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, DH key exchange is typically used in conjunction with a digital "
"signature algorithm to ensure that each party uses an authenticated public "
"key for creating their shared secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya naman, ang DH key exchange ay karaniwang ginagamit kasabay ng isang "
"digital signature algorithm para masiguro na ang bawat partido ay gumagamit "
"ng authenticated na public key para sa paglikha ng kanilang shared secret.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Ang Digital Signature Algorithm (DSA) {#the-digital-signature-algorithm-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even though generic cryptosystems like [RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255) provide digital signature functionality, in 1994 NIST adopted a specialized signature scheme based on modular exponentiation and the discrete logarithm problem as the federal standard for digital signatures. This scheme, which came to be known simply as the [*Digital Signature Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522) (DSA), involves four distinct phases:\n"
"1. **Key generation**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit na ang mga generic na cryptosystem tulad ng "
"[RSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=RSA_(cryptosystem)&oldid=1163962255)"
" ay nagbibigay ng digital signature functionality, noong 1994 ay nag-adopt "
"ang NIST ng isang espesyalisadong signature scheme batay sa modular "
"exponentiation at ang discrete logarithm problem bilang federal standard "
"para sa mga digital signature. Ang scheme na ito, na naging kilala bilang "
"[*Digital Signature "
"Algorithm*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" (DSA), ay nagsasangkot ng apat na magkakaibang phase:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   DSA keys are generated from:\n"
"     - 2 primes that meet certain rules\n"
"       -   $p$ - typically 256 bits (we'll call this length $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - typically 3072 bits (we'll call this length $L$)\n"
"     - A cryptographic hash function that will convert from strings of length $L$ to $N$\n"
"     - An additional Parameters $g$ (see details below)\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang mga DSA key ay nabuo mula sa:\n"
"     - 2 prime na nakakatugon sa ilang partikular na patakaran\n"
"       -   $p$ - karaniwang 256 bits (tatawagin nating ang haba na ito ay $N$)\n"
"       -   $q$ - karaniwang 3072 bits (tatawagin nating ang haba na ito ay $L$)\n"
"     - Isang cryptographic hash function na mag-co-convert mula sa mga string na may haba $L$ sa $N$\n"
"     - Isang karagdagang parameter $g$ (tingnan ang mga detalye sa ibaba)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   From this we choose a random number $x$ as private key, and are able to "
"calculate a public key $y$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Mula dito, pumipili tayo ng random na numero $x$ bilang private key, at "
"makakakalkula tayo ng public key $y$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of key generation\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na detalye ng key generation\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameter generation:** Mathematically, DSA involves a cyclic subgroup of "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ generated by an element $g$ of prime order q < "
"p. The first step in the DSA is therefore to select two primes p, q to set "
"up the necessary mathematical structures.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parameter generation:** Sa matematika, ang DSA ay nagsasangkot ng isang "
"cyclic subgroup ng $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ na nabuo ng isang elemento "
"$g$ ng prime order q < p. Ang unang hakbang sa DSA ay samakatuwid pumili ng "
"dalawang prime p, q para magtayo ng mga kinakailangang matematikal na "
"istruktura.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an $N$-bit prime $q$.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng isang $N$-bit prime $q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose an $L$-bit prime $p$ such that $p-1$ is a multiple of $q$. The choice"
" of $p$ specifies the group $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng isang $L$-bit prime $p$ na $p-1$ ay multiple ng $q$. Ang pagpili "
"ng $p$ ay nagtatakda ng group $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pick an integer $1 < h < p-1$ at random and compute $g = h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$."
" If $g=1$ which happens rarely, try another h.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng isang integer $1 < h < p-1$ nang random at kalkulahin ang $g = "
"h^{(p-1)/q}~mod~p$. Kung ang $g=1$ na bihirang mangyari, subukan ang ibang "
"h.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $g^q~mod~p = 1$. g is thus a generator of a cyclic subgroup "
"$\\langle g \\rangle$ of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ of prime order q.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-verify na ang $g^q~mod~p = 1$. Ang g ay kaya isang generator ng isang "
"cyclic subgroup $\\langle g \\rangle$ ng $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ ng "
"prime order q.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The parameters $(q, p, g)$ specify an instance of the algorithm and are"
" public information. Typically, $ N \\sim 256$ and $L \\sim 3072$ in "
"realistic applications.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Ang mga parameter $(q, p, g)$ ay nagtatakda ng isang instance ng "
"algorithm at pampublikong impormasyon. Karaniwang, ang $ N \\sim 256$ at $L "
"\\sim 3072$ sa mga makatotohanang aplikasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"     The protocol also requires a cryptographic hash function $H : "
"\\{0,1\\}^L \\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ that maps binary $L$-bit strings to "
"$N$-bit strings, for example, SHA-256.\n"
msgstr ""
"     Ang protocol ay nangangailangan din ng isang cryptographic hash "
"function $H : \\{0,1\\}^L \\rightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^N$ na nagma-map ng mga "
"binary $L$-bit na string sa mga $N$-bit na string, halimbawa, SHA-256.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key-pair generation:** The signer needs to generate a key pair on their "
"end.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Key-pair generation:** Kailangang bumuo ang signer ng isang key pair sa "
"kanilang dulo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a random secret integer $ x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. $x$ is the private"
" key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng isang random na lihim na integer $x \\in \\{1,2...q-1\\}$. Ang $x$"
" ay ang private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '     - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generate $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$. $y$ is the signer's public key.\n"
msgstr "Bumuo ng $y = g^{x}~mod~p$. Ang $y$ ay ang public key ng signer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The following information is shared with anyone who wishes to validate a signature\n"
"   - The parameters used $(p,q,g)$ which describe the algorithm\n"
"   - The hash function $H$\n"
"   - the public key $y$\n"
"1. **Signing:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang sumusunod na impormasyon ay ibinabahagi sa sinumang nais mag-validate ng isang signature\n"
"   - Ang mga parameter na ginamit $(p,q,g)$ na naglalarawan ng algorithm\n"
"   - Ang hash function $H$\n"
"   - Ang public key $y$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer can now sign a message $m$. The resulting signature is $(r,s)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na ngayong pirmahan ng signer ang isang mensahe $m$. Ang resultang "
"signature ay $(r,s)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The message and signature are both now sent to the recipient\n"
msgstr "Ang mensahe at signature ay parehong ipinapadala sa tatanggap\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of signing a message\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na detalye ng pagpirma ng mensahe\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "   The signer signs a message $m$ as follows:\n"
msgstr "   Pinirmahan ng signer ang mensahe $m$ tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a secret integer k at random from $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng lihim na integer k nang random mula sa $\\{1,2...q-1\\}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. In the rare instance when $r=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang $r = (g^k~mod~p)~mod~q$. Sa bihirang pagkakataon na $r=0$, "
"subukan ang ibang random k.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. In a rare instances if $s=0$, try "
"another random k.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q$. Sa bihirang pagkakataon na "
"$s=0$, subukan ang ibang random k.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is the tuple $(r, s)$.\n"
msgstr "Ang signature ay ang tuple $(r, s)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The signer transmits the message $m$ as well as the signature $(r,s)$ to the"
" verifier.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinadadala ng signer ang mensahe $m$ pati na rin ang signature $(r,s)$ sa "
"verifier.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Because both $r, s$ are integers, modulo $q$ the signature size is on the"
" order of $N$-bits and not the longer $L$-bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Dahil parehong integer ang $r, s$, modulo $q$ ang laki ng signature ay "
"nasa order ng $N$-bits at hindi ang mas mahabang $L$-bits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"2. **Verification:**\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
"4. **Verification:**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The recipient now wishes to verify the authenticity of the sender.\n"
"   They have access to the public information $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   They can execute a calculation which proves that the sender had access to the private key $x$\n"
msgstr ""
"   Nais ngayon ng tatanggap na i-verify ang pagiging tunay ng nagpadala.\n"
"   Mayroon silang access sa pampublikong impormasyon $(q, p, g, H, y, (r,s), m)$\n"
"   Maaari silang magsagawa ng isang kalkulasyon na nagpapatunay na ang nagpadala ay may access sa private key $x$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   and seeks to ascertain that the signer is someone with access to the "
"private key $x$.\n"
msgstr ""
"   at nagsisikap na matiyak na ang signer ay may access sa private key "
"$x$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of DSA verification scheme\">\n"
msgstr ""
"   <Accordion>\n"
"   <AccordionItem title=\"Matematikal na detalye ng DSA verification scheme\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Verify that $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ and $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, that is, $r, s$ are "
"valid modulo~q integers.\n"
msgstr ""
"I-verify na ang $0 \\lt r \\lt q$ at $0 \\lt s \\lt q$, iyon ay, ang $r, s$ "
"ay mga valid na modulo~q integer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang $u_2 = rw~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compute $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The signature is verified if $v = r$.\n"
msgstr "Ang signature ay na-verify kung ang $v = r$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   For legitimate signatures, the correctness of the DSA algorithm is easily"
" demonstrated as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Para sa mga lehitimong signature, ang kawastuhan ng DSA algorithm ay "
"madaling ipakita tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the signer's end: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = ((H(m) + "
"xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa dulo ng signer: $s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr))~mod~q \\implies k = ((H(m) + "
"xr)s^{-1})~mod~q $\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Considering the right-hand side of the latter equality, a verifier can "
"compute $s^{-1}, H(m)$ because $s, q, m, H$ are public information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang kanang bahagi ng huli na pagkakatumbas, maaaring "
"kalkulahin ng verifier ang $s^{-1}, H(m)$ dahil ang $s, q, m, H$ ay "
"pampublikong impormasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Thus, the verifier computes $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ and $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q = "
"H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, kinakalkula ng verifier ang $w = s^{-1}~mod~q$ at $u_1 = H(m)w~mod~q ="
" H(m)s^{-1}~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The verifier also computes $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ as $r$ is also "
"public.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kinakalkula rin ng verifier ang $u_2 = rw~mod~q = rs^{-1}~mod~q$ dahil ang "
"$r$ ay pampubliko rin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Note that $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"
msgstr "Pansinin na ang $k = (u_1 + xu_2)~mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, a verifier does not have access to $x$ as it is the signer's "
"private key, so $k$ itself cannot be directly computed.  - The scheme "
"instead relies on the fact that even as the verifier cannot compute $k$, "
"with a legitimate signer, the verifier should instead be able to re-compute "
"$(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ with the help of the signer's public key $y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, ang verifier ay walang access sa $x$ dahil ito ang private key "
"ng signer, kaya ang $k$ mismo ay hindi direktang makakalkula.  - Sa halip, "
"ang scheme ay umaasa sa katotohanan na kahit hindi makalkula ng verifier ang"
" $k$, sa isang lehitimong signer, ang verifier ay dapat na makapag-re-"
"compute ng $(g^k~mod~p)~mod~q = r$ sa tulong ng public key ng signer na $y ="
" g^{x}~mod~p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, the verifier computes $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, kinakalkula ng verifier ang $v = (g^{u_1}y^{u_2}~mod~p)~mod~q = "
"(g^{u_1}g^{xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = (g^{u_1+xu_2}~mod~p)mod~q = "
"(g^k~mod~p)mod~q$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '   - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows because $g$ has order $q$ and establishes $v = r$ "
"for valid signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling pagkakatumbas ay sumusunod dahil ang $g$ ay may order $q$ at "
"nagtatag ng $v = r$ para sa mga valid na signature.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"   </AccordionItem>\n"
"   </Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Illustration of the DSA in Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"
msgstr "Ilustrasyon ng DSA sa Python {#illustration-of-the-dsa-in-python}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this example, we'll use small primes to illustrate the DSA process in a "
"scenario where Alice sends a signed message to Bob. We'll use small integers"
" in this example. A real-world scenario would employ much larger primes on "
"the order of 2048-3072 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa halimbawang ito, gagamit tayo ng maliliit na prime number para mailarawan"
" ang proseso ng DSA sa senaryo kung saan nagpapadala si Alice ng "
"nilalagdaang mensahe kay Bob. Gagamit tayo ng maliliit na integer dito. Sa "
"tunay na mundo, gumagamit ng mas malalaking prime number na nasa hanay ng "
"2048–3072 bits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You can try rerunning this example with different values to see how the algorithm behaves, but ensure you start running from the first cell in this section.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Maaari mong subukang patakbuhin muli ang halimbawang ito gamit ang iba't ibang halaga para makita kung paano kumikilos ang algorithm, ngunit tiyaking sisimulan mo mula sa unang cell ng seksyong ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start by importing necessary libraries and choosing our parameters.\n"
"The integer parameters $p$, $q$, $g$ are public information, and satisfy the following rules:\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsisimula tayo sa pag-import ng mga kinakailangang library at pagpili ng ating mga parameter.\n"
"Ang integer na mga parameter na $p$, $q$, $g$ ay pampublikong impormasyon, at dapat matugunan ang mga sumusunod na panuntunan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$p$, $q$ are both prime\n"
msgstr "$p$, $q$ ay parehong prime\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"
msgstr "$(p-1) \\mod\\ q = 0$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\ge 2$\n"
msgstr "$g \\ge 2$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"
msgstr "$g \\le (p-2)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"
msgstr "$g^{(p-1)/q} \\mod\\ p \\neq 1$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next the signer, Alice, generates her private key.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, bubuo si Alice, ang pumipirma, ng kanyang pribadong key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key, k (`alice-private-key` in the python code) must satisfy:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pribadong key na $k$ (`alice-private-key` sa Python code) ay dapat matugunan ang:\n"
" - $k \\ge 2$\n"
" - $k \\le (q-1)$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice keeps her private key secret.\n"
msgstr "Itinatago ni Alice ang kanyang pribadong key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice computes her public key using modular exponentiation. Inverting "
"this step to recover the private key is an instance of the DLP, so difficult"
" to compute on classical computers where large primes are used.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, kinokompute ni Alice ang kanyang pampublikong key gamit ang modular"
" exponentiation. Ang pag-invert ng hakbang na ito para mabawi ang pribadong "
"key ay isang halimbawa ng DLP, kaya mahirap itong kalkulahin sa mga klasikal"
" na computer kung saan gumagamit ng malalaking prime number.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the math explanation above, we know is this can be calculated using the"
" formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mula sa paliwanag ng matematika sa itaas, alam natin na maaari itong "
"kalkulahin gamit ang formula:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"
msgstr "$y = g^{x} \\mod\\ p$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As usual, Alice makes her public key available over a not-necessarily secret"
" channel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng dati, ginagawa ni Alice ang kanyang pampublikong key na available "
"sa pamamagitan ng isang channel na hindi kailangang maging lihim.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now Alice can sign a message.\n"
msgstr "Maaari na ngayong pumirma si Alice ng mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the digital signature scheme, we need to generate a hash $H(m)$ of the "
"message $m$ to be signed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa digital signature scheme, kailangan nating bumuo ng hash na $H(m)$ "
"ng mensaheng $m$ na pipirmahan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's assume Alice and Bob agree to use a particular hashing algorithm with "
"hash length $N$ equal to the number of bits in $q$. In this simple example, "
"we will bound the outputs of our mock hash function by $q$. The hash "
"function here is trivial, simply generating a random integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay nating nagkasundo sina Alice at Bob na gumamit ng partikular na "
"hashing algorithm na may hash length na $N$ na katumbas ng bilang ng bits sa"
" $q$. Sa simpleng halimbawang ito, hahangganin natin ang mga output ng ating"
" mock hash function sa $q$. Ang hash function dito ay trivial — simpleng "
"bumubuo ng random na integer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, Alice needs to generate a random per-message secret number $k$ as well"
" as its multiplicative inverse modulo $q$ to compute the signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, kailangang bumuo si Alice ng random na per-message secret number na"
" $k$ pati na rin ang multiplicative inverse nito modulo $q$ para makapag-"
"compute ng lagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple brute-force algorithm can be used to compute the modular inverse. "
"However it's better to use one of the built-in Python function `pow` as "
"shown below\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring gumamit ng simpleng brute-force algorithm para i-compute ang "
"modular inverse. Gayunpaman, mas mainam na gamitin ang isa sa built-in na "
"Python function na `pow` tulad ng ipinapakita sa ibaba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now compute the signature.\n"
msgstr "Maaari na ngayong i-compute ni Alice ang lagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr "$r = (g^{k} \\mod p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"
msgstr "$s = (k^{-1} (H(m) + xr)) \\mod q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that there are some particular conditions that will require us to "
"choose a different value for $k$ in the case where either $r$ or $s$ compute"
" to $0$. In this case we will generate a new value and repeat.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na may ilang partikular na kondisyon na magpapailangan sa atin na "
"pumili ng ibang halaga para sa $k$ sa kaso kung saan ang $r$ o $s$ ay nag-"
"compute sa $0$. Sa kasong ito, bubuo tayo ng bagong halaga at uulitin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice broadcasts the message and her signature to the receiver or verifier, "
"Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini-broadcast ni Alice ang mensahe at ang kanyang lagda sa tatanggap o "
"verifier, si Bob.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Bob has previously intercepted Alice's public key and can now verify the "
"signature to authenticate her message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nakuha na dati ni Bob ang pampublikong key ni Alice at maaari na ngayong "
"i-verify ang lagda para ma-authenticate ang kanyang mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To do so, he performs some checks, and then re-generates a hash of Alice's broadcast message and computes the auxiliary quantities $w, u_1, u_2$ and $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para magawa ito, nagsasagawa siya ng ilang pagsusuri, pagkatapos ay muli niyang bubuuin ang hash ng broadcast na mensahe ni Alice at kinokompute ang mga auxiliary quantity na $w, u_1, u_2$ at $v$.\n"
"- $0 < r < q$\n"
"- $0 < s < q$\n"
"- $w = s^{-1} \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{1} = H(m) . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $u_{2} = r . w \\mod\\ q$\n"
"- $v = (g^{u1}y^{u2} \\mod\\ p) \\mod\\ q$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob checks if $v$ equals $r$. If they are equal, then the signature"
" is verified.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, sinusuri ni Bob kung katumbas ng $r$ ang $v$. Kung magkapantay "
"sila, napatunayan na ang lagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Security of the DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"
msgstr "Seguridad ng DSA {#security-of-the-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With classical computing, the security of the DSA can be influenced by "
"several factors:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa klasikal na computing, ang seguridad ng DSA ay maaaring maimpluwensyahan "
"ng ilang salik:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key size**: As always, key size provides basic protection against brute "
"force attacks. Modern applications that use DSA use key sizes of at least "
"2048 bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Laki ng key**: Tulad ng palagi, ang laki ng key ay nagbibigay ng "
"pangunahing proteksyon laban sa brute force attacks. Ang mga modernong "
"aplikasyon na gumagamit ng DSA ay gumagamit ng key size na hindi bababa sa "
"2048 bits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Quality of $k$**: In DSA, each signature needs a unique, random, and "
"secret $k$ value (see above). The uniqueness, entropy, and secrecy of $k$ "
"are critical, and weakness in any of these aspects could lead to the private"
" key $x$ being compromised. The random number generators used for generating"
" $k$ need to be secure themselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kalidad ng $k$**: Sa DSA, ang bawat lagda ay nangangailangan ng natatangi,"
" random, at lihim na halaga ng $k$ (tingnan sa itaas). Ang pagiging "
"natatangi, entropy, at pagiging lihim ng $k$ ay kritikal, at ang kahinaan sa"
" alinman sa mga aspetong ito ay maaaring makompromiso ang pribadong key na "
"$x$. Ang mga random number generator na ginagamit para bumuo ng $k$ ay "
"kailangang maging ligtas din ang mga ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Hash function strength**: Since DSA uses a hash function as part of the "
"signature generation and verification process, a weak hash function could "
"compromise the security of the digital signature. For example, the use of "
"SHA-1 with DSA is deprecated and SHA-2 or higher is recommended.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Lakas ng hash function**: Dahil gumagamit ang DSA ng hash function bilang "
"bahagi ng proseso ng pagbuo at pag-verify ng lagda, ang isang mahinang hash "
"function ay maaaring makompromiso ang seguridad ng digital signature. "
"Halimbawa, ang paggamit ng SHA-1 kasama ng DSA ay deprecated na at "
"inirerekomenda ang SHA-2 o mas mataas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these, robust DSA implementation should also guard against "
"other types of attacks that target asymmetric key cryptography as previously"
" outlined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa mga ito, ang matibay na implementasyon ng DSA ay dapat ding mag-"
"ingat laban sa iba pang uri ng pag-atake na nagta-target sa asymmetric key "
"cryptography tulad ng dati nang binanggit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#authenticated-key-"
"exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr ""
"Authenticated key exchange gamit ang Diffie-Hellman at DSA {#authenticated-"
"key-exchange-with-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern network security protocols, such as [Transport Layer Security "
"(TLS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" and many others, involve combining the functionalities of key exchange and "
"authentication. In the context of Diffie-Hellman, authentication is needed "
"to guard against MITM attacks. In the following code cells, we illustrate an"
" example where Alice and Bob perform an authenticated key exchange by "
"combining the Diffie-Hellman and DSA protocols. For this, we will use the "
"`cryptography` Python library.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga modernong network security protocol, tulad ng [Transport Layer "
"Security "
"(TLS)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531)"
" at marami pang iba, ay kinabibilangan ng pagsasama ng mga functionality ng "
"key exchange at authentication. Sa konteksto ng Diffie-Hellman, kailangan "
"ang authentication para maprotektahan laban sa mga MITM attack. Sa mga "
"sumusunod na code cell, inilarawan natin ang isang halimbawa kung saan "
"nagsasagawa sina Alice at Bob ng authenticated key exchange sa pamamagitan "
"ng pagsasama ng mga protocol na Diffie-Hellman at DSA. Para dito, gagamitin "
"natin ang `cryptography` na Python library.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and "
"DSA](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/asymmetric-key-"
"cryptography/auth_key_exchange.svg)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange with Diffie-Hellman and DSA*\n"
"First, Alice and Bob agree on a set of DH parameters and generate a set of DH public-private key pairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Figure 2. Authenticated key exchange gamit ang Diffie-Hellman at DSA*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys are broadcast. Next, both Alice and Bob each generate a "
"separate key pair for use with DSA. These keys will in turn be used to sign "
"the DH public keys to be exchanged.\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, nagkakasundo sina Alice at Bob sa isang hanay ng mga DH parameter at "
"bumubuo ng isang hanay ng DH public-private key pair.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice signs her DH public key using her DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini-broadcast ang mga DH public key. Susunod, parehong bumubuo sina Alice at"
" Bob ng hiwalay na key pair para gamitin sa DSA. Ang mga key na ito ay "
"gagamitin naman para lagdaan ang mga DH public key na ipagpapalitan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, Bob signs his DH public key using his DSA private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nilalagdaan ni Alice ang kanyang DH public key gamit ang kanyang DSA private"
" key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The DH public keys and corresponding signatures are now broadcast by both "
"Alice and Bob. Having received their counterparty's public key and "
"signature, each party then verifies the signature is valid. This way, a MITM"
" attack can be prevented, as Alice, for instance, knows that Bob's DH public"
" key was indeed signed by Bob and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayundin, nilalagdaan ni Bob ang kanyang DH public key gamit ang kanyang DSA"
" private key.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Following signature verification, Alice and Bob generate the shared secret, "
"which completes the key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga DH public key at kaukulang mga lagda ay ini-broadcast na ngayon ng "
"parehong Alice at Bob. Pagkatanggap ng pampublikong key at lagda ng kanilang"
" katapat, bine-verify ng bawat partido na valid ang lagda. Sa ganitong "
"paraan, mapipigilan ang MITM attack, dahil alam ni Alice, halimbawa, na ang "
"DH public key ni Bob ay talagang nilagdaan ni Bob at kabaliktaran.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally, for additional security, Alice and Bob can use a specialized key"
" derivation function such as *HKDF* to generate a more secure symmetric key "
"from their shared secret using *key stretching* techniques.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos ng pag-verify ng lagda, bumubuo sina Alice at Bob ng shared "
"secret, na nagkukumpleto sa key exchange.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking Diffie-Hellman and DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"
msgstr "Pagsira sa Diffie-Hellman at DSA {#breaking-diffie-hellman-and-dsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) and "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" protocols involve the generation of public keys of the form $ y = "
"g^{x}~mod~p$, where the private key $x$ is the discrete logarithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Parehong ang [Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman_key_exchange&oldid=1163912552)"
" (DH) at "
"[DSA](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1148950522)"
" na mga protocol ay kinabibilangan ng pagbuo ng mga pampublikong susi na may"
" anyo na $ y = g^{x}~mod~p$, kung saan ang pribadong susi $x$ ay ang "
"discrete logarithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An attacker who can solve an instance of the DLP can expose the private key "
"of one of the two parties and, by combining it with the public key of the "
"second party, get access to the shared secret. In the case of DSA, an "
"attacker who can solve the DLP can recover the signer's private key, voiding"
" the basic premise of a digital signature.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang umaatake na kayang solusyunan ang isang instance ng DLP ay "
"maaaring ilantad ang pribadong susi ng isa sa dalawang partido at, sa "
"pamamagitan ng pagsasama nito sa pampublikong susi ng pangalawang partido, "
"makakuha ng access sa shared secret. Sa kaso ng DSA, ang isang umaatake na "
"kayang solusyunan ang DLP ay maaaring makuha ang pribadong susi ng nagpirma,"
" na nagpapawalang-bisa sa pangunahing saligan ng isang digital na lagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On classical computing systems, the DLP is believed not to have a "
"polynomial-time solution. But as shown by Peter Shor in his [original 1994 "
"paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), Shor's algorithm also "
"solves the DLP in polynomial-time on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga klasikal na sistema ng computing, ang DLP ay pinaniniwalaang walang "
"solusyon sa polynomial na oras. Ngunit tulad ng ipinakita ni Peter Shor sa "
"kanyang [orihinal na papel noong "
"1994](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700), ang algorithm ni Shor ay "
"naglulusot din sa DLP sa polynomial na oras sa mga quantum computer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm and the discrete logarithm problem {#shors-algorithm-and-"
"the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Ang algorithm ni Shor at ang discrete logarithm problem {#shors-algorithm-"
"and-the-discrete-logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm is able to solve the discrete logarithm problem in "
"polynomial time. It primarily achieves its efficiency by using quantum "
"algorithms which can find the period of a function which depends on the "
"input to the problem - which is then combined with more conventional "
"operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya ng algorithm ni Shor na solusyunan ang discrete logarithm problem sa "
"polynomial na oras. Pangunahing nakukuha nito ang kahusayan sa pamamagitan "
"ng paggamit ng mga quantum algorithm na kayang hanapin ang period ng isang "
"function na nakadepende sa input ng problema — na pinagsama pagkatapos sa "
"mas karaniwang mga operasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical details of Shor's algorithm\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mga mathematical na detalye ng algorithm ni Shor\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Shor's algorithm provides an efficient solution to the DLP by mapping it to "
"a more general problem in group theory known as the [hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ang algorithm ni Shor ng mahusay na solusyon sa DLP sa "
"pamamagitan ng pag-map nito sa mas pangkalahatang problema sa group theory "
"na kilala bilang [hidden subgroup "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hidden_subgroup_problem)"
" (HSP).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the HSP, one is given an algebraic group $G$ and a function $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$  from $G$ to some set $X$ such that $f$ is constant on each "
"coset of some subgroup $H$ of $G$ (and distinct on different cosets). Then, "
"the task is to determine $H$. It is known that quantum computers can solve "
"the HSP on finite Abelian groups in time polynomial in $log~|G|$ where $|G|$"
" is the group order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa HSP, ibinibigay ang isang algebraic group $G$ at isang function $f: G "
"\\rightarrow X$ mula sa $G$ patungo sa ilang set $X$ na kung saan ang $f$ ay"
" constant sa bawat coset ng ilang subgroup $H$ ng $G$ (at natatangi sa iba't"
" ibang cosets). Pagkatapos, ang gawain ay tukuyin ang $H$. Alam na ang mga "
"quantum computer ay kayang solusyunan ang HSP sa mga finite Abelian group sa"
" oras na polynomial sa $log~|G|$ kung saan ang $|G|$ ay ang order ng "
"grupo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the case of the integer DLP discussed in this lesson, the mapping to the "
"HSP is as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kaso ng integer DLP na tinalakay sa araling ito, ang pag-map sa HSP ay "
"ganito:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $p$ be a prime and consider the DLP given by $ y = g^r~mod~p$ where $g$ "
"is a generator of $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Since $g^{p-1} \\equiv "
"1~mod~p$, $g$ has order $p-1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hayaan na ang $p$ ay isang prime at isaalang-alang ang DLP na ibinigay ng $ "
"y = g^r~mod~p$ kung saan ang $g$ ay isang generator ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$. Dahil ang $g^{p-1} \\equiv 1~mod~p$, ang $g$ ay"
" may order $p-1$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ where "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ is the group of integers modulo $(p-1)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng $G = \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ kung saan ang "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{p-1}$ ay ang grupo ng mga integer modulo $(p-1)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ given as $f(a, b) = "
"g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng $f : G \\rightarrow (\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ na ibinigay bilang "
"$f(a, b) = g^a y^{-b}~mod~p \\equiv g^{a-rb}~mod~p$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The kernel of $f$ is then the subgroup $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle = "
"\\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang kernel ng $f$ ay ang subgroup na $H_0 = \\langle (r, 1) \\rangle = "
"\\{(a,b) \\in G | f(a,b) \\equiv 1~mod~p\\} = \\{ (a, b) \\in G | a - rb "
"\\equiv 0~mod~(p-1)\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$f$ is constant on the cosets $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ and \"hides\" the "
"subgroup $H_0$ setting up an HSP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $f$ ay constant sa mga coset na $(\\delta, 0) + H_0$ at \"itinatago\" "
"ang subgroup $H_0$ na nagtatayo ng isang HSP.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the above, Shor's quantum algorithm for the integer DLP uses a quantum"
" oracle to evaluate the function $f$ on a state representing a uniform "
"superposition over $G$, and then uses the <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A "
"quantum algorithm that can be used to find periodic patterns. Named after "
"the Fourier transform in classical physics which can split a signal into a "
"set of sine waves.\">quantum Fourier transform</DefinitionTooltip> and "
"measurements with <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm used "
"to estimate phase in qubits, named after phase estimation in classical "
"physics.\">phase estimation</DefinitionTooltip> to produce quantum states "
"that allow for the identification of the generator $(r, 1)$ of $H_0$. From "
"this, $r$, the discrete logarithm of interest, can be extracted.\n"
msgstr ""
"Batay sa nabanggit, ang quantum algorithm ni Shor para sa integer DLP ay "
"gumagamit ng quantum oracle para suriin ang function $f$ sa isang estado na "
"kumakatawan sa uniform superposition sa ibabaw ng $G$, at pagkatapos ay "
"gumagamit ng <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm that can be"
" used to find periodic patterns. Named after the Fourier transform in "
"classical physics which can split a signal into a set of sine "
"waves.\">quantum Fourier transform</DefinitionTooltip> at mga sukat na may "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"A quantum algorithm used to estimate phase "
"in qubits, named after phase estimation in classical physics.\">phase "
"estimation</DefinitionTooltip> upang makagawa ng mga quantum state na "
"nagbibigay-daan sa pagkilala ng generator na $(r, 1)$ ng $H_0$. Mula rito, "
"ang $r$, ang discrete logarithm na kinauukulan, ay maaaring makuha.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Shor's original paper](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) has a "
"detailed description of the algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [orihinal na papel ni Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) ay"
" may detalyadong paglalarawan ng algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Elliptic curve cryptography {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr "Elliptic curve cryptography {#elliptic-curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[*Elliptic curve cryptography "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), based on the mathematics of [*elliptic"
" "
"curves*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" offers a powerful approach to asymmetric key cryptography. ECC is known to "
"provide a similar level of security as methods such as RSA but with shorter "
"keys, making it more efficient and particularly well suited to systems with "
"limited resources, such as embedded systems and mobile devices, where the "
"[storage and computational savings of smaller key sizes are highly "
"desirable](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [*Elliptic curve cryptography "
"(ECC)*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993), batay sa matematika ng mga [*elliptic "
"curve*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664),"
" ay nag-aalok ng makapangyarihang paraan para sa asymmetric key "
"cryptography. Kilala ang ECC na nagbibigay ng katulad na antas ng seguridad "
"tulad ng mga pamamaraan gaya ng RSA ngunit may mas maikling mga susi, na "
"ginagawa itong mas mahusay at partikular na angkop sa mga sistema na may "
"limitadong mapagkukunan, tulad ng mga embedded system at mobile device, kung"
" saan ang [pagtitipid sa imbakan at pagkukuwenta mula sa mas maliliit na "
"sukat ng susi ay lubhang kanais-"
"nais](https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2018.2881444).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic principles of elliptic curve cryptography {#basic-principles-of-"
"elliptic-curve-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Mga pangunahing prinsipyo ng elliptic curve cryptography {#basic-principles-"
"of-elliptic-curve-cryptography}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An elliptic curve is typically of the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with a few interesting properties.\n"
"* It is horizontally symmetric. So for any point $(x,y)$ on the curve, it's reflection $(x,-y)$ is also on the curve\n"
"* Any non-vertical strain line will only intersect the curve at a maximum of three points\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang elliptic curve ay karaniwang may anyo na $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ na may ilang kawili-wiling katangian.\n"
"* Ito ay pahalang na simetriko. Kaya para sa anumang punto $(x,y)$ sa kurba, ang kanyang repleksyon na $(x,-y)$ ay nasa kurba rin.\n"
"* Anumang hindi vertical na tuwid na linya ay magtatawid lamang sa kurba sa maximum na tatlong punto.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b> ](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/asymmetric-key-cryptography/ECCfig.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Operations of addition and point doubling on an elliptic curve. "
"Facet 1 defines <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Facet 2 illustrates point doubling <b>2Q "
"= -P</b>. Facet 3 defines the additive inverse of a point as its reflection "
"about the x-axis i.e, <b>P = -Q</b>*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Larawan 1. Mga operasyon ng pagdaragdag at point doubling sa isang elliptic"
" curve. Ang Facet 1 ay nagtatakda ng <b>P + Q = -R</b>. Ang Facet 2 ay "
"naglalarawan ng point doubling na <b>2Q = -P</b>. Ang Facet 3 ay nagtatakda "
"ng additive inverse ng isang punto bilang repleksyon nito sa x-axis, i.e, "
"<b>P = -Q</b>*\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography makes use of applying a series of arithmetic "
"operations to points on the curve. Each effectively navigates to a new point"
" on the curve. This is a simple process to follow in one direction, and with"
" shorter key sizes is more efficient than other algorithms like RSA, but "
"trying to reverse this is very difficult, hence its application to "
"cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang elliptic curve cryptography ay gumagamit ng paglapat ng isang serye ng "
"mga aritmetikong operasyon sa mga punto sa kurba. Bawat isa ay epektibong "
"nagdadala sa isang bagong punto sa kurba. Ito ay isang simpleng prosesong "
"sundan sa isang direksyon, at sa mas maikling sukat ng susi ay mas mahusay "
"kaysa sa iba pang mga algorithm tulad ng RSA, ngunit ang pagsubok na "
"baligtarin ito ay napakahirap, kaya naman ginagamit ito sa cryptography.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical principles of elliptic curve cryptography\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mga mathematical na prinsipyo ng elliptic curve cryptography\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An [elliptic "
"curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" over an algebraic field $K$ is defined by a mathematical equation, "
"typically in the form $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ with the coefficients $a, b \\in "
"K$ and describes points $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ with the additional "
"requirement that the curve have no kinks or self-intersections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang [elliptic "
"curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve&oldid=1164567664)"
" sa isang algebraic field $K$ ay tinukoy ng isang mathematical equation, "
"karaniwang may anyo na $y^2 = x^3 + ax + b$ na may mga coefficient na $a, b "
"\\in K$ at naglalarawan ng mga punto $(x, y) \\in K \\otimes K$ na may "
"karagdagang kinakailangan na ang kurba ay walang mga kink o self-"
"intersection.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The properties of elliptic curves allow for operations of \"addition\" and "
"\"scalar multiplication\" to be defined involving points on the curve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga katangian ng mga elliptic curve ay nagpapahintulot na ang mga "
"operasyon ng \"addition\" at \"scalar multiplication\" ay matukoy na "
"kinabibilangan ng mga punto sa kurba.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Addition**: If $P$ and $Q$ are two points on an elliptic curve, then $P + "
"Q$ describes a unique third point identified as follows: Draw the line that "
"intersects $P$ and $Q$ and find the third point, $R$, at which the line "
"intersects the curve again. We then define $P + Q =  −R$, the point opposite"
" $R$ reflected through the $x$-axis (see figure below) . When the line "
"through $P, Q$ does not intersect the curve at any finite $(x, y)$, we say "
"it intersects the curve at the point at infinity $\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Addition**: Kung ang $P$ at $Q$ ay dalawang punto sa isang elliptic curve,"
" ang $P + Q$ ay naglalarawan ng isang natatanging ikatlong punto na "
"natutukoy tulad ng sumusunod: Iguhit ang linyang dumadaan sa $P$ at $Q$ at "
"hanapin ang ikatlong punto, $R$, kung saan muling tumatawid ang linya sa "
"kurba. Tinutukoy natin na $P + Q = −R$, ang puntong salungat kay $R$ na "
"sinasalamin sa $x$-axis (tingnan ang pigura sa ibaba). Kapag ang linyang "
"dumadaan sa $P, Q$ ay hindi tumatawid sa kurba sa anumang finite na $(x, "
"y)$, sinasabi nating ito ay tumatawid sa kurba sa punto sa infinity na "
"$\\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve addition satisfies algebraic **group** properties with the "
"point at infinity as the additive identity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang elliptic curve addition ay nakakatugon sa algebraic **group** na mga "
"katangian na may punto sa infinity bilang additive identity.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Doubling and scalar multiplication:** The operation of point doubling "
"which corresponds to scalar multiplication by $2$ is obtained by setting $P "
"= Q$ in the addition operation and graphically involves the tangent line at "
"$P$. General scalar multiplication by an integer $n$ defined as $nP =  P + P"
" + ...~n$ times is obtained by repeated doubling and addition.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Doubling at scalar multiplication:** Ang operasyon ng point doubling na "
"tumutugma sa scalar multiplication ng $2$ ay nakuha sa pamamagitan ng "
"pagtatakda ng $P = Q$ sa operasyon ng addition at grapikal na kinabibilangan"
" ng tangent line sa $P$. Ang pangkalahatang scalar multiplication ng isang "
"integer $n$ na tinukoy bilang $nP = P + P + ...~n$ beses ay nakuha sa "
"pamamagitan ng paulit-ulit na doubling at addition.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem {#elliptic-curve-discrete-"
"logarithm-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem {#elliptic-curve-discrete-"
"logarithm-problem}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem (ECDLP) has many similarities "
"to the discrete logarithm problem discussed previously, being based around "
"the challenges of finding factors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang elliptic curve discrete logarithm problem (ECDLP) ay may maraming "
"pagkakatulad sa discrete logarithm problem na tinalakay dati, batay sa mga "
"hamon ng paghahanap ng mga factor.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation of [scalar multiplication on elliptic "
"curves](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" allows for the definition of the [elliptic curve discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993):\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyon ng [scalar multiplication sa mga elliptic "
"curve](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_curve_point_multiplication&oldid=1145917191)"
" ay nagpapahintulot sa kahulugan ng [elliptic curve discrete logarithm "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_cryptography&oldid=1160709993):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given points $P, Q$ on an elliptic curve such that $Q = nP$, determine "
"$n$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ibinibigay ang mga punto $P, Q$ sa isang elliptic curve na kung saan ang $Q "
"= nP$, tukuyin ang $n$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This problem is known to be intractable on classical computers for large $n$"
" and provides a basis for cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang problemang ito ay kilala na hindi malulutas sa mga klasikal na computer "
"para sa malaking $n$ at nagbibigay ng batayan para sa cryptographic "
"security.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of ECDLP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical na paglalarawan ng ECDLP\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Elliptic curve cryptography is primarily based on the ECDLP formulated on "
"certain algebraic **finite fields**. In 1999, NIST recommended ten finite "
"fields for use in ECC. These are:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang elliptic curve cryptography ay pangunahing batay sa ECDLP na ginawa sa "
"ilang algebraic **finite field**. Noong 1999, nagrerekomenda ang NIST ng "
"sampung finite field para gamitin sa ECC. Ito ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **prime fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ for primes $p$ of size $\\{192, "
"224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Limang **prime field** na $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$ para sa mga prime $p$ na may "
"sukat na $\\{192, 224, 256, 384, 521\\}$ bits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Five **binary fields** $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ for $n \\in \\{163, 233, 283,"
" 409, 571\\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Limang **binary field** na $\\mathbb {F} _{2^{n}}$ para sa $n \\in \\{163, "
"233, 283, 409, 571\\}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With the above setup, an ECC-based asymmetric key cryptosystem in the case "
"of **prime fields** may be specified as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa itaas na setup, ang isang ECC-based asymmetric key cryptosystem sa kaso "
"ng **prime field** ay maaaring tukuyin tulad ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a $p$ from the NIST-recommended list of values to specify $\\mathbb "
"{F} _{p}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng $p$ mula sa listahan ng mga halagang inirerekomenda ng NIST upang "
"tukuyin ang $\\mathbb {F} _{p}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Select parameters $a, b$ of the elliptic curve.\n"
msgstr "Pumili ng mga parameter na $a, b$ ng elliptic curve.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a **base point** $G$ which \"generates\" a cyclic subgroup on the "
"curve with order $n$; that is, the smallest integer such that $nG = "
"\\mathbf{O}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pumili ng **base point** na $G$ na \"gumagawa\" ng cyclic subgroup sa kurba "
"na may order na $n$; iyon ay, ang pinakamaliit na integer na kung saan ang "
"$nG = \\mathbf{O}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calculate the **cofactor** $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ where $|E(\\mathbb"
" {F} _{p})|$ is the number of points on the curve. $h$ is typically a small "
"integer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kalkulahin ang **cofactor** na $h = |E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|/n$ kung saan ang "
"$|E(\\mathbb {F} _{p})|$ ay ang bilang ng mga punto sa kurba. Ang $h$ ay "
"karaniwang isang maliit na integer.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **domain parameters** $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ allow the specification of "
"asymmetric keys in this way:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang **domain parameters** na $(p, a, b, G, n, h)$ ay nagpapahintulot sa "
"pagtukoy ng mga asymmetric key sa ganitong paraan:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The private key is a randomly chosen integer $d$ with as many bits as in the"
" prime $p$. It should be kept secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pribadong susi ay isang random na piniling integer $d$ na may "
"kasinlaking bits tulad ng prime $p$. Dapat itong panatilihing lihim.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The public key is the result of \"multiplying\" the base point $G$ by the "
"private key $d$. This is typically denoted as $Q = dG$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pampublikong susi ay ang resulta ng \"pagpaparami\" ng base point $G$ ng"
" pribadong susi $d$. Ito ay karaniwang tinutukoy bilang $Q = dG$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recovering $d$ is equivalent to solving the ECDLP, which is assumed to be "
"intractable for large $d$. The ECDLP therefore forms the basis for key "
"exchange and digital signature schemes in direct analogy with the Diffie-"
"Hellman and DSA schemes defined over $(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ discussed "
"previously.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagbawi ng $d$ ay katumbas ng paglutas ng ECDLP, na ipinapalagay na "
"hindi malulutas para sa malaking $d$. Ang ECDLP ay nagsisilbing batayan para"
" sa key exchange at digital signature scheme sa direktang pagkakatulad sa "
"mga Diffie-Hellman at DSA scheme na tinukoy sa ibabaw ng "
"$(\\mathbb{Z}_p)^{\\times}$ na tinalakay dati.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key exchange with ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Key exchange gamit ang ECC {#key-exchange-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One of the primary uses of ECC is in the key exchange protocol known as "
"[elliptic curve Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). In ECDH, each party "
"generates a private-public key pair and then exchanges public keys. Each "
"party then uses their own private key and the other party's public key to "
"compute a shared secret, which can be used as the key for symmetric "
"encryption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isa sa mga pangunahing gamit ng ECC ay sa key exchange protocol na kilala "
"bilang [elliptic curve Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic-"
"curve_Diffie%E2%80%93Hellman&oldid=1160050860) (ECDH). Sa ECDH, bawat "
"partido ay bumubuo ng isang private-public key pair at pagkatapos ay "
"nagpapalitan ng mga pampublikong susi. Bawat partido ay gumagamit ng "
"kanilang sariling pribadong susi at ng pampublikong susi ng kabilang partido"
" upang kalkulahin ang isang shared secret, na maaaring gamitin bilang susi "
"para sa symmetric encryption.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While it's relatively easy to perform point addition on an elliptic curve "
"and derive a public key from a private key, it's computationally infeasible "
"to reverse the process and derive a private key from a public key. This "
"\"one-way\" behavior provides the security of the ECDH key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang medyo madali itong magsagawa ng point addition sa isang elliptic "
"curve at makuha ang isang pampublikong susi mula sa isang pribadong susi, "
"ito ay computationally infeasible na baligtarin ang proseso at makuha ang "
"isang pribadong susi mula sa isang pampublikong susi. Ang \"one-way\" na "
"gawi na ito ang nagbibigay ng seguridad sa ECDH key exchange.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we will illustrate an example of how one might perform an ECDH key "
"exchange using Python and the library `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito, maglalatag tayo ng halimbawa kung paano maaaring magsagawa ng ECDH key"
" exchange gamit ang Python at ang library na `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Digital signatures with ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"
msgstr "Mga digital na lagda gamit ang ECC {#digital-signatures-with-ecc}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"ECC can also be used to generate digital signatures using the [Elliptic "
"Curve Digital Signature "
"Algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). In ECDSA, the signer creates a signature using their private key, "
"and others can verify the signature using the signer's public key. Just like"
" with ECDH, the security of ECDSA relies on the ECDLP. It's computationally "
"infeasible for someone to forge a signature without access to the signer's "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari ring gamitin ang ECC upang makabuo ng mga digital na lagda gamit ang "
"[Elliptic Curve Digital Signature "
"Algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Elliptic_Curve_Digital_Signature_Algorithm&oldid=1162097661)"
" (ECDSA). Sa ECDSA, lumilikha ang naglalagda ng lagda gamit ang kanilang "
"pribadong susi, at maaaring i-verify ng iba ang lagda gamit ang pampublikong"
" susi ng naglalagda. Tulad ng ECDH, ang seguridad ng ECDSA ay nakasalalay sa"
" ECDLP. Hindi posible na computationally ang magpeke ng lagda nang walang "
"access sa pribadong susi ng naglalagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following is an example of a simple sign-and-verify transaction using "
"ECDSA with Python and `cryptography`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod ay isang halimbawa ng simpleng sign-and-verify na transaksyon "
"gamit ang ECDSA na may Python at `cryptography`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the above code, if one modifies the message after it has been signed, the"
" verification will fail, providing a guarantee of authenticity and integrity"
" for the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa code sa itaas, kung babaguhin ng isa ang mensahe pagkatapos itong "
"mapirmahan, ang pag-verify ay mabibigo, na nagbibigay ng garantiya ng "
"pagiging tunay at integridad ng mensahe.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Breaking ECDH and ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"
msgstr "Pagsira sa ECDH at ECDSA {#breaking-ecdh-and-ecdsa}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In an analogous way to the integer discrete logarithm problem, the ECDLP "
"turns out to be hard on classical computers but has an efficient solution on"
" quantum computers once again via Shor's algorithm. We refer you to recent "
"literature for a discussion related to [generalizing Shor's algorithm to the"
" ECDLP case](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa katulad na paraan sa integer discrete logarithm problem, ang ECDLP ay "
"lumalabas na mahirap sa mga klasikal na computer ngunit may mahusay na "
"solusyon sa mga quantum computer muli sa pamamagitan ng algorithm ni Shor. "
"Itinuturo namin kayo sa kamakailang literatura para sa talakayan na may "
"kaugnayan sa [pagpapalawig ng algorithm ni Shor sa kaso ng "
"ECDLP](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-89432-0_8).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Buod {#summary}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we started by looking at the main characteristics of "
"asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) and discussed basic security "
"considerations that underpin asymmetric cryptosystems. In particular, we "
"introduced the two main applications of AKC — namely, key exchange and "
"digital signatures — both of which are essential components of modern "
"internet-based communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa araling ito, nagsimula tayo sa pagtingin sa mga pangunahing katangian ng "
"asymmetric key cryptography (AKC) at tinalakay ang mga pangunahing "
"pagsasaalang-alang sa seguridad na nagtataglay ng mga asymmetric "
"cryptosystem. Sa partikular, ipinakilala natin ang dalawang pangunahing "
"aplikasyon ng AKC — iyon ay, ang key exchange at mga digital na lagda — "
"parehong mahalagang bahagi ng modernong komunikasyong batay sa internet.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at the RSA cryptosystem, which since the 1970s, has proven to"
" be of immense value for securing modern digital communications by enabling "
"key exchange and digital signatures within a simple and versatile framework."
" The cryptographic security of RSA with respect to classical computing is "
"based on the hardness of factoring large integers and requires key sizes in "
"the range of 2048 bits to assure the integers used in practical applications"
" are large enough to resist factorization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, tumingin tayo sa RSA cryptosystem, na mula pa noong 1970s, ay "
"napatunayang napakahalaga para sa pagse-secure ng modernong digital na "
"komunikasyon sa pamamagitan ng pagbibigay-daan sa key exchange at mga "
"digital na lagda sa loob ng isang simple at versatile na balangkas. Ang "
"cryptographic security ng RSA kaugnay ng klasikal na computing ay batay sa "
"kahirapan ng factoring ng malalaking integer at nangangailangan ng mga sukat"
" ng susi na nasa hanay ng 2048 bits upang matiyak na ang mga integer na "
"ginagamit sa mga praktikal na aplikasyon ay sapat na laki para labanan ang "
"factorization.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then looked at Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange and the Digital Signature"
" Algorithm (DSA). The security of these schemes is predicated on the integer"
" discrete logarithm (DLP) problem, the private key being computationally "
"hard to extract given the public key, with no polynomial time solution on "
"classical computers. Use of random and unique keys affords additional "
"security against attacks. Both the integer finite field and elliptic curve "
"variants of the DH and DSA protocols currently find widespread use across "
"many modern digital communications protocols such as "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" and so on.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagkatapos, tumingin tayo sa Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange at ang Digital"
" Signature Algorithm (DSA). Ang seguridad ng mga scheme na ito ay nakabatay "
"sa integer discrete logarithm (DLP) problem, ang pribadong susi ay "
"computationally mahirap na kunin batay sa pampublikong susi, na walang "
"solusyon sa polynomial na oras sa mga klasikal na computer. Ang paggamit ng "
"mga random at natatanging susi ay nagbibigay ng karagdagang seguridad laban "
"sa mga pag-atake. Parehong ang integer finite field at elliptic curve na mga"
" variant ng DH at DSA protocol ay kasalukuyang malawakang ginagamit sa "
"maraming modernong digital na komunikasyon protocol tulad ng "
"[*TLS*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Transport_Layer_Security&oldid=1155601531),"
" "
"[*SSH*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Secure_Shell&oldid=1158549718),"
" at iba pa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally we looked at Elliptic curve cryptography. With its efficient key "
"size and strong security properties, it currently represents an excellent "
"choice for many cryptographic applications, from key exchange to digital "
"signatures.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, tumingin tayo sa Elliptic curve cryptography. Sa mahusay na sukat "
"ng susi at matibay na mga katangian ng seguridad, ito ay kasalukuyang "
"kumakatawan sa isang mahusay na pagpipilian para sa maraming cryptographic "
"na aplikasyon, mula sa key exchange hanggang sa mga digital na lagda.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of these algorithms have exposure to attack from quantum algorithms, "
"since solutions can be developed to solve the mathematical problems which "
"acted as a premise in their design. One such example is Shor's algorithm. "
"Therefore they will need to be replaced by quantum-safe asymmetric "
"cryptosystems which are more resilient to attack from quantum - as well as "
"being as safe with classical algorithms. The mathematical problems they rely"
" on can be solved efficiently by quantum computers, necessitating the "
"development of quantum-safe asymmetric cryptosystems that can withstand "
"quantum attacks while maintaining classical security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lahat ng mga algorithm na ito ay nakalantad sa pag-atake mula sa mga quantum"
" algorithm, dahil maaaring bumuo ng mga solusyon upang malutas ang mga "
"mathematical na problema na nagsilbing saligan sa kanilang disenyo. Isang "
"halimbawa nito ay ang algorithm ni Shor. Kaya naman, kailangang palitan ang "
"mga ito ng mga quantum-safe asymmetric cryptosystem na mas matibay laban sa "
"pag-atake mula sa quantum — pati na rin ang pagiging ligtas sa mga klasikal "
"na algorithm. Ang mga mathematical na problema na kanilang inaasahan ay "
"maaaring malutas nang mahusay ng mga quantum computer, na nangangailangan ng"
" pagbuo ng mga quantum-safe asymmetric cryptosystem na kayang labanan ang "
"mga quantum na pag-atake habang pinapanatili ang klasikal na seguridad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A future lesson will look at quantum-safe cryptosystems and discuss the "
"required approach to maintain cryptographic security.\n"
msgstr ""
